{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show a518cbb:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.controller.review.md'","aggregated_output":"<!-- Reviewer: Codex gpt-6.2-sol, effort max (observed in the session rollout, thread 01a1ecf0-d286-7880-bb18-f201e69b367f), read-only, cross-provider. Reviewed commit 4809516. -->\n\n**Four defects block release at `4809516`.** A superseded frame can change the figure, Resume can remove the source rows of marks still on screen, a renderer exception can leave layers on different revisions, and a stream with `keep` can grow without bound when frames stop running.\n\n**Ran** means reproduced in Node with the manual frame host unless otherwise stated. **Reasoned** means traced through the source or tests.\n\n## Blocking\n\n1. **B · A superseded frame writes to the figure. Ran.** Draw data at x `[0,2]`, then update the title and data to `Intermediate` and `[5,7]`. Have a readout formatter call a second update for `[10,12]`. After one frame, the figure says `Intermediate` and the prepared controls use `[5,7]`, but the marks and committed lookup still use `[0,2]`. A formatter that calls `destroy()` also lets `figure.update()` run after host disposal. The lazy `reader.summary` runs author code inside the call to `figure.update()`, past the generation check. Plan §1.5 and DX5 require a single revision across the layers. Materialize formatter-dependent output before writing it, then check the generation before each host mutation that follows author code. [controller.ts](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:935)\n\n2. **B · Resume releases rows that the displayed lookup still needs. Ran on all five chart types.** Display a store-backed line window `[2,3]`, pause, and append `4` with `keep: 1`. Hovering `2` while paused returns its original row. Resume and hover again before the frame runs. The same mark and source index now return `row: null`. I also reproduced the loss when an append was pending at the time of Pause. The controller freezes `accepted.frame`, which can differ from the displayed frame, and discards the frozen rows in `accept()` before the replacement draws. This breaks plan §1.5, DX2 and DX5. Keep row ownership with the displayed snapshot until the replacement completes, including across Pause, Resume and re-encoding. [Freezing rows](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:550) · [Accepting the replacement](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:403)\n\n3. **B · An actual renderer exception can leave the marks, lookup and error message out of sync. Ran.** Draw `[0,2]`, then make the host text renderer throw and update to `[5,7]`. The new marks draw, the old interaction model remains, and the error message never appears. `showInternal()` retries the broken text renderer before clearing interaction or updating the figure. With a persistently throwing mark renderer, the error message appears over the old marks because clearing them calls the same renderer. Both recovered after restoring the host method and updating again. L7 and DX5 require a complete error revision. Disable interaction first, isolate each cleanup step, and let the host hide failed render surfaces independently of their draw methods. [Frame publication](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1055) · [Error fallback](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1117)\n\n4. **B · `keep` fails to bound a stream without successful frames. Ran.** Create a line with three rows and leave its first frame queued. After 1,000 one-row appends with `keep: 3`, the store reports **1,003 retained rows**. After 100 appends with `keep: 2` and a forced reader failure on every frame, it reports **102**. Retirement depends on the successful frame path. A zero-size flush has another problem. It commits new controls and retires the old source with the mark draw count unchanged. Plan §1.5 and P7 require bounded retention with correct provenance. Pin the displayed snapshot, release superseded pending revisions as calls arrive, and explicitly clear the display if an unmeasured or failed frame is going to release its source. [Draw and retirement](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1034) · [Failed frames](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1107)\n\n## Major\n\n5. **M · Re-encoding exposes paused arrivals, and a failed Resume loses the pending frame. Ran.** Pause a line displaying `[1,2,3]`, append `4` with `keep: 3`, then update `y` to another valid field. The chart shows `[2,3,4]` with Pause still active. In a second run, forcing the view stage to throw on Resume consumed the held frame. Removing the fault and making a valid title update recovered the chart without the buffered row. I6 and plan §1.5 require accepted arrivals to stay buffered until Resume. Re-encode the displayed and pending windows separately, and clear the pending frame only after its replacement is accepted. [Re-encoding](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:479) · [Resume](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:640)\n\n6. **M · Append validation writes to the wrong state. Ran.** A first strict append containing `NaN` throws AX103 but queues a frame and flips the chart’s streaming controls on. On a paused chart, adding series nine or donut slice nine leaves AX130 or AX121 out of `diagnostics` until Resume. `update({strict:true})` succeeds in between. In the other direction, a negative donut value buffered while paused adds AX120 immediately, then an unrelated resize applies that error to the previously healthy displayed ring. Plan §1.5, I6 and §3.5 require synchronous validation, rollback on strict rejection, and disclosure for the data being drawn. Set the streaming flag on acceptance and keep complete validation findings for the pending snapshot and display effects for the displayed snapshot. [Append transaction](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:523) · [Display state](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:721)\n\n7. **M · Re-entrant calls drop diagnostic and event deliveries. Ran.** On a strict chart, submit an update that raises AX103 and AX106. If the first `onDiagnostic` call makes a valid title update, the exception contains both codes but the callback and console receive only AX103. With two `zoom` subscribers, have the first respond to `[0.5,2]` by calling `zoom([1,2])`. The second subscriber receives only `[1,2]`. A title update from the first hover subscriber also suppresses the second. This breaks call-order delivery and §3.5 reporting. Drain each delivery snapshot in order, queue nested notifications behind it, and stop on destruction. Keep nested calls’ validation and state changes synchronous. [Diagnostic delivery](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:329) · [Event delivery](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1174)\n\n8. **M · A valid append cannot clear a stale missing-field error. Ran on all five types.** Create a non-strict chart with one row missing the entire value field. Append a row with that field and `keep: 1`. AX101 and the error message remain. Scatter and donut already have a usable retained frame at that point. Line, area and bar still have an empty frame. The append carries the original option validation forward, and the aligned store can open with the invalid encoding. F3, DX5 and §3.5 require diagnostics for the current data. Revalidate field presence when the retained logical table changes, and let a now-valid table rebuild the invalid frame. [Static diagnostics retention](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:474) · [Opening and appending to the store](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:515)\n\n9. **M · Late setup failure and retained unsubscribe functions leave resources alive. Reasoned for browser setup. Ran for the watcher and unsubscribe paths.** If `ResizeObserver.observe()` throws after the controller is created, `createChart()` releases the host but skips `controller.handle.destroy()`. The first frame is already queued. In Node, a fake window throwing on the second `matchMedia()` call left the first listener registered. Separately, keeping one unsubscribe function after `destroy()` kept another subscriber’s captured object alive through forced collection. Releasing that function made the object collectible. DX5 and P7 require teardown of pending work and subscriptions. Destroy the controller on late setup failure, register watcher cleanup as each subscription succeeds, and clear or invalidate individual subscription records on destruction. [Browser setup](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:109) · [Late catch](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:193) · [Unsubscribe closure](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1290)\n\n10. **M · Two charts on one target overwrite each other’s colors. Reasoned.** Create two SVG charts on the same element and pin their first series to red and blue respectively. Both bind slot one through the same custom property on the target, so the second chart changes the first chart’s paint. Destroying either chart can remove or restore properties still in use by the other. The cleanup also records only the presence of a pre-existing `data-axylo-scheme`, so it cannot restore its value after a scheme change. This breaks DX6 and DX5. Scope the chart-written theme properties and scheme attribute to the chart’s own figure. [Property cleanup](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:77) · [Theme target](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:190)\n\n11. **M · Ordinary stream operations copy, scan or retain old data. Ran.** A subsequent one-row append on a 50,001-row line replaced both numeric buffers despite spare capacity. A title-only update allocated a 50,001-entry row index synchronously with the normalization counter unchanged. The reader also rescans unchanged statistics when rebuilding the caption. In a forced-GC probe, the original caller columns survived both `keep: 2` and explicit data replacement. They became collectible when a locale change rebuilt the formatter cache. Plan §2.2, the frame ownership contract and AGENTS.md require incremental appends and cheap presentation changes. Prepare append deltas over shared storage, resolve presentation changes without walking retained rows, cache statistics by view, and keep cached formatter callbacks free of table-bearing state. [Presentation update](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:492) · [Append preparation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:535) · [Buffer fork](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:52) · [Formatter closure](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:762)\n\n12. **M · Resubmitting edited options can leave the old output in place. Ran.** Change a reference’s position, a pinned color, a message and an axis label on objects previously supplied to the chart. Pass those objects back in `update()`. The reference, theme, message and axis title all stay stale. The previous options and cache keys hold the same mutable objects. With a fresh object, a label-only or unit-only edit instead reruns normalization and view construction. Plan §1.5 and §2.2 require present keys to take effect and presentation changes to invalidate the right stages. Snapshot small option inputs independently of borrowed data, then update field metadata without rebuilding the value columns. [Patch storage](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/options.ts:19) · [Encoding comparison](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/stages.ts:47) · [Theme key](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:831)\n\n13. **M · AX160 can disappear, duplicate or survive its cause. Ran.** A readout formatter that always throws reports AX160 on the first frame. Replacing the data with the same formatter clears the diagnostic and reader note even though fallback formatting continues. An invalid `Intl` option combination reports nothing because formatter construction raises AX160 immediately before the controller clears the bucket. Using the same throwing function for ticks and readouts produces two identical entries. Removing both formatters while switching to an error state leaves the tick warning and note behind. This violates F6, F12 and §3.5. Associate findings with the active formatter and layout outputs, clear a bucket before rebuilding its producer, and retire findings from inactive outputs. [Formatter cache](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:847) · [Layout cache](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:964) · [Once-only readout reporter](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/format/number.ts:155)\n\n14. **M · A create-stage exception bypasses AX199 delivery and breaks `validate()` parity. Ran.** Create with a row whose x getter throws during normalization. The controller shows its generic error, but `onDiagnostic` receives nothing and `chart.diagnostics` is empty, even with strict enabled. `validate()` classifies the same exception as AX150. There is also a parity difference on all five types with `palete: undefined`: `validate()` reports AX150, while create discards the key during patch processing. Plan §1.5, §1.6 and spec §3.5 require shared call validation and error delivery. Use one preprocessing and classification path, and retain initial failure diagnostics independently of an accepted frame. Apply strict handling according to the phase where the finding arose. [Controller error handling](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:435) · [Diagnostic getter](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:291) · [Static validation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/stages.ts:140)\n\n15. **M · Scatter drops the declared percentage scale when computing the domain. Ran.** Create a scatter with y values `20` and `63` and `y.scale: 'percent'`. The upper bound is `70`, although F7 requires `100`. Tick formatting receives the scale, but the controller’s scatter view state omits it. Pass the resolved value scale into that branch and assert the domain for both `percent` and `ratio`. [Scatter view state](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/stages.ts:67) · [Scatter domain calculation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:329)\n\n16. **M · A zoom at the latest bar or scatter datum can stop following. Ran.** For scatter at x `0` and `9`, zoom to `[5,9]` and append `12`. The window stays `[5,9]`. For continuous bars at `0,5,10`, zoom to `[5,10]` and append `15`. That window also stays put. The controller tests the niced or padded `xFull` edge rather than the newest datum. Plan §1.5 requires the live window to follow the data edge. Determine whether the window follows from the latest data position, then clamp the shifted window to the author’s bounds. [Edge detection](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:205) · [Append follow logic](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:538)\n\n17. **M · Category zoom changes the visible rows without changing the axis. Ran for line and area.** Create categories A–D and call `zoom(['B','C'])`. The view limits picking and rows to B and C, but layout still emits four ticks on a four-band projection and the controller exposes no zoom controls. This leaves the chart’s geometry inconsistent with its visible range under plan §1.5 and the spec §3.6 type matrix. Use the same ordinal window and offset for the projection, ticks, marks and lookup, and enable controls for supported category charts. [Category layout](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:103) · [Zoom controls](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:925)\n\n18. **M · An all-missing bar window suppresses the required missing marks. Ran.** Create bars `A: null` and `B: null`. The table contains both rows, but the controller shows “No data to show” and sends an empty scene. Its readiness check requires a finite value even though the bar scene can draw missing glyphs at the baseline. F2 requires those glyphs. Treat retained missing bar slots as drawable and reserve the empty state for a window with no drawable slots. [Display classification](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:721) · [Drawable-content check](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1368)\n\n19. **M · Environment changes can be missed or cause two draws in one frame. Ran the callback sequences. Reasoned through browser wiring.** After drawing at DPR 1, change the host to DPR 3 and signal reattachment. The committed ratio stays 1 until a separate DPR notification. Reattachment also leaves the font epoch alone, so a font load missed while detached can leave cached widths in use. Changing only the document’s `lang` has no watcher. Conversely, executing the scheduled data update and then the theme watcher’s callback produces two draws in the same frame callback batch. Plan §2.2, F5, F6 and the renderer contract require fresh environment inputs and one mark draw per animation frame. Refresh inputs on reattachment, watch language changes, and feed theme invalidation into the same frame scheduler. [Controller invalidation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1211) · [Reattachment](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:109) · [Theme watcher](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/watch.ts:11)\n\n20. **m · Several regression tests can pass when the behavior named in the test is broken. Reasoned from assertions. Ran the host accessor check.** The Node re-entrancy test receives AX140 before its `chart` variable is assigned, so its nested update never runs. The dense-line test reads indices recomputed by `__bench.describe()`, so it can pass with a broken scene. The browser crossing test checks only that the message is hidden, and the `plotRole` test supplies no role override. The browser teardown test can pass with listeners still registered because the destroyed controller suppresses their effects. The setup-failure test throws before any frame is scheduled. The stand-in’s `Object.assign` also snapshots `pending` and `layout`, so those properties cannot verify frame timing. Assert actual output and listener registration, and exercise the missing sequences directly. Within the scoped files I found no test for a stream receiving appends with **zero** frame callbacks, Resume-to-first-frame row provenance, late setup failure, or two live charts on the same target. [Controller tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/controller.test.ts:170) · [Dense-line test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/controller.test.ts:579) · [Host accessors](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/host.ts:143) · [Browser review tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review.browser.test.ts:175) · [Setup failure test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review.browser.test.ts:316) · [Plot role test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review.browser.test.ts:493) · [Teardown test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/lifecycle.browser.test.ts:285)\n\n## Verification\n\nI reviewed the created, pending-first-frame, drawn, paused, failed and destroyed states across static and streaming instances of all five types. I checked call-time validation and diagnostics separately from frame-time marks, labels and lookup. The stage probes covered data and encoding, field presentation, domains and references, chart variants and visibility, caption and controls, locale and time zone, colors, resize, fonts and DPR. I exercised all 14 stage failure hooks, plus actual throwing host render methods and author callbacks.\n\nThe review was read-only. I loaded the exact commit into memory for the Node probes and ran the core Vitest suite in the thread pool with both caches disabled. The browser tests were inspected only. Browser rendering, native observer behavior and the full P7 heap budget remain unverified. I used the donut label as its `keep` key and read §3.6 as including category zoom for line and area. The proposed fixes fit the existing fixed contracts.\n\n```text\nTest Files  8 passed (8)\n     Tests  86 passed (86)\n  Start at  05:47:13\n  Duration  528ms (transform 63%, tests 19%, import 16%, worker 1%)\n```\n\n## Areas examined and found sound\n\n- **Ordinary call order, ran.** Data replacement, append and applicable zoom before the first frame produced one draw. A subsequent explicit data replacement discarded the stream.\n- **Fresh option patches, ran.** Whole-object replacement restored omitted nested defaults, explicit `undefined` restored the top-level default, and absent keys kept their values.\n- **Static ownership, ran.** Clean, ascending `Float64Array` x and y columns were borrowed for all four Cartesian types in the tested fixtures. Donut borrowed its value column. Appending left the caller’s values unchanged.\n- **Ordinary strict rejection, ran.** A rejected strict create disposed its host before drawing. The ninth-series test preserved the previous data through a later valid append. Invalid strict zoom reported AX107 without throwing or moving the window.\n- **Attached environment and layout caches, ran.** Explicit locale and time-zone changes reached the formatter, font notifications invalidated measurements, and data replacement with unchanged tick inputs reused layout.\n- **Ordinary destruction and callback exceptions, ran.** Repeated destroy disposed once, canceled the first frame, and made later calls inert. Throwing author handlers left the chart usable.\n- **Registry coverage, reasoned.** Every §3.5 code has an emission path, and I found no emitted AX code outside the registry.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
