nts`, `normalizeDonut`. The stores and `reader/x.ts` now call these directly.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:26:- `data/store.ts`: `openAlignedStore`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:27:- `data/store-unaligned.ts`: `openPointStore`, `openDonutStore`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:28:- `view/index.ts`: `buildAlignedView`, `buildScatterView`, `buildDonutView`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:29:- `scene/index.ts`: `cartesianScene` plus `line`/`area`/`bar`/`scatter` layers and scenes, and `donutScene`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:30:- `lookup/index.ts`: `*LookupFor` functions.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:31:- `reader`: `readerWith(parts)`, with `alignedReader`, `scatterReader` and `donutReader`; the table is split per shape.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:32:- `core/focus.ts`: `overlayWith(targetMarks)`, with aligned, scatter and donut target marks.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:33:- `dom/interaction.ts`: `InteractionParts` (overlay, swatch, `stepInSeries`, `donutSliceList`).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:34:- `dom/swatch.ts`: `swatchPattern`, so bar pattern drawing is reached only from `barSwatch`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:35:- `render/svg.ts` and `render/canvas.ts`: per-mark handler tables. `createSvgRenderer` and `createCanvasRenderer` still have every handler.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:38:- I measured both options. With all import-time work removed, prebundled and a module graph (one file per source module, `sideEffects` false) came out within 25 B for every kind.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:39:- The module graph was 5.7 KB better for `validate` alone, but only while the stylesheet template still did work at import.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:40:- I chose prebundled because it leaves `exports`, `files`, the declarations and the package-shape tests unchanged.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:43:- marker polygons are now built lazily;\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:44:- computed constants (2π, 2⁻²⁰, squares) became literals;\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:45:- the registry became plain data, with the message composed in `createDiagnostic`;\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:46:- the option-name lists are written out instead of spread;\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:47:- `Intl.Segmenter` is created on first use;\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:48:- the time-interval table is built lazily;\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:49:- `TOKEN_BINDINGS` is no longer `Object.freeze`d (readonly by type only; nothing mutates it);\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:50:- the stylesheet is a literal (step 2).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:53:- Importing `axylo` only for its effects, with `ignoreAnnotations` set so esbuild ignores `sideEffects`, bundles to 0 bytes.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:54:- For each kind, the bundle must contain its own markers and none of the other kinds'. The markers survive minification:\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:61:- Each marker is first required in its own kind's bundle, so a marker lost to a rename fails the test instead of passing everything.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:65:### Step 2: stylesheet minified once\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:66:- New `src/theme/minify.ts` removes only comments and layout whitespace. It keeps commas, colons, values and strings, and drops the `;` before `}`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.report.md:67:- `scripts/build.mjs` substitutes the minified literal for `theme/css.ts` in `axylo.js` and `axylo.iife.min.js`, and writes the same text to `dist/axylo.css`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tree-shake.