-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:9:- **Where it applies:** when the datum's floating tooltip is not across the reading axis (beside a bar or stack; always on scatter and donut).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:10:- **Hold:** after a rest, the datum is held while the pointer is inside the convex hull of the resting point and the tooltip's rectangle. Leaving the hull resumes picking on that same move; a pointer that never rested is never held. The tooltip stays pointer-transparent and does not move.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:11:- **One adjustment:** the corridor opens on the first move after the rest, even a move of 2 px or less. Without that, a datum resting exactly on a band edge (the acceptance bar probe) changed on the first 1 px step.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:12:- **Tests:** five browser tests in `test/browser/chart/review6.browser.test.ts`:\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:21:### 2. L4 on a prefers-color-scheme change, fixed in CSS (`src/theme/`)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:22:- **Stylesheet (`css.ts`):** the `.axylo` private defaults are now `light-dark(light, dark)`, so they switch in the frame the media query does. Fixed sets remain under `[data-axylo-scheme=\"light\"]` and `[data-axylo-scheme=\"dark\"]`. The comment says `light-dark()` is supported by the current and previous major versions of the four browsers in spec 2.3.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:23:- **Resolution (`resolve.ts`):** when the chart's computed `color-scheme` is anything but `normal` and no `--axylo-background` decides, no `data-axylo-scheme` is written. The per-series properties were already references, not frozen colours.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:26:- **Canvas:** it still repaints when the change event arrives, one frame behind; a comment in `controller.ts` says so, and AX141 is judged then.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:27:- **Tests:**\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:30:- **Tests changed:** three render tests and two of my chart tests expected the attribute in \"page sets color-scheme\" cases. They now expect none, which is the design change, not a loosened check.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:32:### 3. Two-tone focus ring (palette review B1)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:33:- **Datum ring (`core/focus.ts`):** a 4 px background-colour surround with the 2 px focus colour on top, i.e. 1 px of background on each side. Corners are closed, the ring is kept inside the plot's box, and the tooltip's avoid-box grows by the surround (`RING_REACH` 10).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:34:- **Plot outline (`css.ts`):** an inset `box-shadow` in the background colour under the 2 px outline. `forced-color-adjust: none` keeps it in forced colours, where both tokens are already system colours.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:35:- **Tests:**\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:38:- The acceptance A2 tests still pass.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:40:### 4. Untitled chart named by its target's id (React review C6)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:41:- `Host.targetId`, from `root.id` in `chart.ts`, is used for the diagnostic chart name and for the internal-error delivery. The allocated id stays for the DOM relationships.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:42:- Node tests in `snapshot.test.ts`: \"sessions\" when the target has that id, the allocated id otherwise. `test/core/host.ts` has a new `targetId` option.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:44:### Edits outside `src/core` and `src/dom`\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:45:- `src/theme/css.ts`: the token blocks and the ring surround.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:46:- `src/theme/resolve.ts`: the scheme attribute rule only.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md:47:- `tes