ongs to the data module |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:23:| 17 (rescoped) | `zoom()` on a category axis or a donut is a no-op reported as AX150 (`field: 'zoom'`). A window kept from a numeric axis never reaches categories | line, area, bar and donut tests \"finding 17\". My partial category-zoom code (band offset, layout offset, whole-category steps) was removed with `git checkout` of my own files |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:25:| 20 (weak tests) | Re-entrancy test now runs its nested update. Dense-line test checks the drawn path. Browser crossing test checks series-colour pixels. `plotRole` test uses an override. A teardown test counts listeners through the DevTools protocol. A late-setup-failure test asserts a frame was requested before the failure | `controller.test.ts`, `review.browser.test.ts`, `lifecycle.browser.test.ts` |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:27:### Documentation author's items\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:39:### Reader review, finding 5\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:42:### Interaction review\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:55:### Edits outside `src/core` and `src/dom`\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:56:- `src/theme/watch.ts`: attribute list reverted (no test needed; the render theme test covers it).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:57:- `src/scale/domain.ts`, `src/scale/index.ts`: `coarserDomains`, tested in `test/scale/domain.test.ts`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:58:- `src/layout/index.ts`, `src/layout/labels.ts`: `ValueAxis.coarser`, `FittedLabels.partial`, and the retry. Tested in `test/layout/layout.test.ts`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:61:- `src/theme/css.ts` (figure section).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:62:- `test/core/host.ts`: new `pageLang` option. Someone else also added `timeZone`, `locale`, `textWidth` and `captionLineHeight` there, and changed `src/index.ts` imports to `./public.js`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:63:- **Shared bundle:** to show tests fail on the old code, I swapped `dist` to the d49e8a8 bundle several times and rebuilt afterwards. Other agents' browser runs in that window may have used the old bundle.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:65:### How to run acceptance on canvas\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:68:### Runs (last lines)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:69:- **Type check:** exit 1. The one error is `packages/axylo/test/acceptance/dx-diagnostics.test.ts(180,9) TS2322`, a file the acceptance agent was editing. An earlier run also showed an error in `src/reader/table.ts`, also edited by another agent.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:70:- **`npm test`:** `Test Files 13 failed | 62 passed (75)`, `Tests 83 failed | 2122 passed (2205)`. Every failure is in `test/acceptance`: 8 of the 13 files are `.scratch/` mutation runs, and the rest are files being edited. The same f-domains, f-donut, f-format, dx-diagnostics, f-stacks and dx-controller tests also fail against the HEAD tree.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:71:- **Node core, scale and layout:** `Test Files 18 passed (18)`, `Tests 284 passed (284)`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:72:- **Browser, my directories, SVG:** `Test Files 12 passed (12)`, `Tests 174 passed (174)`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:73:- **Browser, my directories, canvas:** `Test Files 12 passed (12)`, `Tests 174 passed (174)`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:74:- **Browser acceptance, SVG:** `Test Files 4 failed | 9 passed (13)`, `Tests 14 failed | 455 passed (469)`. That run overlapped my bundle swaps and the suite's own edits. On a stable bundle the failing set is 9 tests (A7 bar sliding window, A10 bar, A2 focus indicators ×5, C4 compact bar, T-tooltip-donut), and the same 9 fail against the HEAD bundle.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core4.fix.report.md:80:### Contract changes\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:3:## Third fix pass: chart core (two third-round reviews, plus the later additions)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:7:### The snapshot design (`core/controller.ts`)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:10:- **Displayed snapshot.** `onScreen` holds the frame on screen, its store and, if needed, a copy of its rows. `drawn` holds the view, layout, lookup and reader for it. It changes only when a frame publishes, and becomes empty after a failed frame or a frame with no size.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:11:- **Row ownership.** `release()` runs after every accepted call and every published frame, whether or not frames run.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:15:- **One generation per frame.** Author code runs, and the lazy `reader.summary`/`note` are materialized, before the first host write. If the chart changed or was destroyed by then, the frame stops having written nothing. Once writing has started, the frame finishes for the same state, and a newer call is drawn by the next frame. A destroyed controller swaps in an inert host.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:16:- **Error revision.** Each step runs on its own, in this order: interaction off, then the error message, then a new host `surfaces(false)` hides marks and text without calling their draw methods, then the content is cleared. The next good frame shows the surfaces again.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:17:- **Held state.** While paused, `diagnostics` include the held rows' findings, but the error state is decided only from what is on screen. A held frame is dropped only once its replacement is accepted, so a failed Resume keeps it and the next accepted call shows it.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:18:- **Notifications.** `onDiagnostic`, console output and events go through one in-order queue. Each delivery is fixed when it is made and delivered in full; only destruction stops it.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:22:### Controller review\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:31:| 5 re-encode while paused / failed Resume | yes (failed Resume) | failed Resume: yes. Re-encode while paused: no | snapshot \"finding 5\" |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:32:| 6 append writes wrong state | yes | yes | snapshot \"finding 6\" ×3 |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:33:| 7 re-entrant deliveries | yes | yes | snapshot \"finding 7\" ×2 |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:34:| 8 stale AX101 after a valid append | not tested | no | — |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:35:| 9 late setup failure / kept unsubscribe | yes (unsubscribe) | yes (controller destroyed on late failure; per-subscription cleanup in `watchEnvironment`) | snapshot \"finding 9\" |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:36:| 10 two charts on one target | yes | yes (theme properties and scheme on the chart's own figure) | review3 \"finding 10\" |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:37:| 11 stream copies / scans | not tested | partly: formatters no longer hold the table. Not done: statistics cached by view, title update without a row-index allocation | — |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:38:| 12 resubmitted mutated objects | not tested | no | — |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:39:| 13 AX160 lifecycle | not tested | no | — |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:40:| 14 create exception → AX199 | yes | yes (delivered before anything is accepted; `validate` classifies the same way; undefined keys handled alike) | snapshot \"finding 14\" |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:41:| 15 scatter percent/ratio domain | yes | yes (`core/stages.ts`) | snapshot \"finding 15\" |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:42:| 16 follow at the latest datum | yes | yes (latest data x, `missingX` included) | snapshot \"finding 16\" ×2, missingX test |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:43:| 17 category zoom | — | no | — |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:44:| 18 all-missing bars | yes | yes | snapshot \"finding 18\" |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:45:| 19 environment changes | not run against 4809516 | yes: DPR and font epoch reread on reattach; `lang` watched; theme changes go through the frame scheduler (one draw per frame) | snapshot \"finding 19\" ×2 |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:46:| 20 weak tests | yes (host accessors) | partly: host keeps live accessors, records surfaces and writes after dispose; Node re-entrancy test rewritten. Other named tests not reworked | — |\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:48:### Interaction review\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:63:- New items 6–10 (too-small/compact focus handoff and overlay reset; Zoom in that can zoom out; misleading slider in loading and all-hidden states; touch-sized row actions; cancelled pinch frame).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:64:- Part 1 items 2 (exact identity for pins and dismissal), 3 (slice list availability), 9 (attainable minimum), 10, 11, 12 (CSS transforms), 13, 15 (shrinking an open table: one test passes, nothing more done).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:65:- Part 3, the list of weak tests.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:69:### Acceptance-suite requests\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:70:- **F4 scatter month/year precision:** fixed (precision read from the caller's rows; the point frame has no field for it).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:71:- **F7 domain ends at a drawn tick:** fixed in `core/axes.ts`, not in scale or layout. Layout may only choose tick sets whose first and last ticks are the domain's ends with no tick between an extreme and its end. Property test `test/core/ticks.test.ts` covers line, bar and scatter for container heights 300–700 px.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:72:- **Below about 200 px of plot F7 can still fail:** five-interval rounding needs more ticks than fit. Fixing that needs the domain chosen in layout with the data extent, a scale/layout change.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:73:- **A4 x unit in the table header:** wired; passes.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:74:- **L3 zero-size:** passes (no draw call before anything was drawn).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:75:- **A10, A5 bar gap, I1 bar, I1 scatter:** pass.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:76:- **L8:** the visible summary is now the first sentence; the full summary moved to a separate description element, still the figure's `aria-describedby`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:77:- **Still failing:**\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:80:- **Messages I build myself:** \"Total\" (tooltip and value text), `pan*`, `jumpNotFound`, `plotInstructions`. None of the sentences `seeTable` affects. The donut slice text joins value and share as `${value} (${percent})` in `dom/interaction.ts`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:82:### Edits outside `src/core` and `src/dom`\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:94:### Last lines of each run\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:95:- **Type check:** `tsc -p packages/axylo` and `tsc -p docs/api` both clean.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:96:- **Node core:** `Tests 114 passed (114)`. Node acceptance: `Tests 494 passed (494)`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:97:- **`npm test`:** `1 failed | 1209 passed`. The one failure is simplify's million-point timing test, not mine.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:98:- **Owned browser directories:** SVG `Tests 163 passed (163)`; canvas `Tests 163 passed (163)`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:99:- **Browser acceptance:** SVG `Tests 5 failed | 452 passed (457)` (the five listed above).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:100:- **Browser acceptance with canvas:** `135 failed`. The suite reads the SVG DOM (`svg.axylo-svg`, `getScreenCTM`). My suite-wide canvas switch in `chart/util.ts` also reaches these tests, so they fail by construction, not because of the library. The suite needs an opt-out or a renderer-agnostic way of reading marks.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:102:### Not observable here\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:103:- Screen-reader speech: decision 0004 part 2, and `aria-valuetext`, which Chrome's accessibility tree does not report (it gives the number).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:104:- Behaviour under CSS transforms.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:105:- Real GPU rasterization.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:107:### Contract changes needed\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:108:- **`DatumRef` comment**, corrected sentence: \"x position (category: its index in the frame that produced the ref; categories can slide when a streaming window evicts them, so a holder remaps by category name across frames of one epoch).\"\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:109:- **Bar cue past 32 series:** `RectMark.pattern` has only three kinds, so series 9 and 33 repeat colour and pattern. Spec F9 needs more pattern kinds in the contract.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:110:- **`plotInstructions` default:** the current default (\"Enter shows one series at a time\") misdescribes the keys. Proposed: \"Left and right arrows move between points, up and down between series, and Enter selects. Plus and minus zoom; 0 resets.\"\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:3:## Chart core, fifth pass: report\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:7:### 1. F7: the domain ends at the first drawn tick at or beyond each extreme\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:8:- **Cause:** a floating-point comparison in `core/axes.ts` `endingCandidates`. The check `b - step < hi` let the 0.1-step tick set through, because 0.2 − 0.1000…09 comes out just below 0.1.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:9:- **Fix:** each tick set is now checked on its own tick values. The first tick at or above the maximum must be the last tick, and the last tick at or below the minimum must be the first. `scale/domain.ts` was already exact.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:10:- **Tests:**\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:15:### 2. Donut shares: at most one fraction digit\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:16:- A new `shareText` in `format/number.ts` is what `formatters.percent` now uses. It rounds the exact decimal, so 0.1235 reads 12.4%.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:17:- Values on a percent or ratio scale keep their F6 readout digits.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:18:- Tests in `test/format/index.test.ts`: 17.2%, the German form, 12.4%, 33.3%, and a ratio value that stays 17.241379%.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:20:### C4: the series colour on the pattern overlay\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:21:- `render/svg.ts` `updateBars`: the overlay rects that carry the pattern also carry the series colour style. The colour is part of the cache key, so a theme change updates it.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:22:- Test in `test/browser/render/review.browser.test.ts`: the elements carrying the series colour whose fill is a pattern. It failed before the fix and passes now; the render suite is 84 passed, 1 skipped.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:24:### 3. Interaction review\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:38:- With 24 px rows everywhere, the hover tooltip grew about 12 px. At two plot edges it then no longer fit beside the mark, so the existing test \"at each of the four plot edges…\" fell back to the readout and failed.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:39:- What I did: rows are 24 px when the tooltip is pinned by a tap, in the fixed readout, and in the slice list. A mouse-hover tooltip keeps text-height rows, which are still buttons.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:40:- So WCAG 2.5.8 is met wherever rows are acted on by touch. It is not met for mouse clicks on hover rows. If you want 24 px rows there too, tell me and I will change the edge test's fixture instead.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:42:### 4. Tests that passed with the behaviour broken\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:43:- Click test (`review2`): now asserts the floating tooltip's title and the exact selected x at each of the four positions.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:44:- Contrast dash test: no longer skips when every plotted SVG path is solid.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:45:- Donut legend: a second fixture where value and share differ, expecting \"3 (60%)\" and \"2 (40%)\".\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:46:- Zoom exclusions: now covers category bar, line, area and donut, by buttons and the `+` key.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:47:- Coarse-double loop in `focus2` (pass 4).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:51:### 5. Reader helper, note runs and AX143\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:52:- The stand-in is gone; the call site imports `seriesNotDrawnSentence` from `../reader`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:53:- `FigureModel.noteSegments` takes the reader's runs. A run is marked `en` only on a page in another language.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:54:- Node test: overriding only `seeTable` leaves \"Siehe Tabelle.\" unmarked; overriding only the sentence marks the built-in \"See table.\" `en`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:55:- `figure.ts` no longer adds spaces between runs; the reader's runs carry their own.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:56:- AX143 now passes `chartType`, `xKind` (taken from the frame for scatter as well) and `horizontal` for bars. Node test: vertical category bars get the horizontal-bar hint, a category line does not.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:58:### 6. Mixed-sign totals\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:63:### Edits outside `src/core` and `src/dom`\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:64:- `src/render/svg.ts`: the C4 change only.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:65:- `src/format/number.ts` and `src/format/index.ts`: share precision only.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:66:- `src/theme/css.ts`: the figure section (choice buttons).\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:67:- Test files: `test/scale/domain.test.ts`, `test/format/index.test.ts`, `test/browser/render/review.browser.test.ts`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:69:### Not done\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:70:- **Item 13 with rule 4 (reserved space for the readout).** Reserving space when the floating tooltip might not fit costs a small tile's plot room on every chart; that is why I reverted it in pass 3. Placing the readout inside the plot column stops it covering the controls but drops \"reserved\". I need a decision: reserve space only below some figure width (which width?), or allow the readout over the plot.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:71:- **Part 3, remaining:**\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:79:### Runs (last lines)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:80:- **Type check:** exit 0.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:81:- **`npx vitest run packages/axylo/test --exclude '**/acceptance/**'`:** `Test Files 2 failed | 43 passed (45)`, `Tests 2 failed | 768 passed (770)`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:84:- **Browser chart and a11y, SVG:** `Test Files 13 passed (13)`, `Tests 184 passed (184)`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:85:- **Browser chart and a11y, canvas:** `Test Files 13 passed (13)`, `Tests 184 passed (184)`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:86:- **Browser render:** `Test Files 5 passed | 1 skipped (6)`, `Tests 84 passed | 1 skipped (85)`.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core5.fix.report.md:87:- **`npx vitest run packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts`:** `Test Files 1 passed (1)`, `Tests 28 passed (28)`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
