{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/02-product-spec.md | sed -n '118,212p'; nl -ba docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md | sed -n '107,131p'\"","aggregated_output":"   118\t| L8 | When the figure cannot hold a readable plot (less than 120×80 CSS px for the plot), it shows the title, a short summary (the first sentence of the generated summary, on at most two lines, cut with an ellipsis beyond that; the full summary remains the figure's description) and the table control instead, and raises AX142. | Narrow and short container tests | R2 |\n   119\t\n   120\t### 3.3 Interaction\n   121\t\n   122\t| ID | Criterion | Verified by | Driven by |\n   123\t|---|---|---|---|\n   124\t| I1 | Pointing anywhere in the plot shows what is there, by the picking rule for the chart type (section 3.6), within one frame at the 95th percentile. On line, area and bar the tooltip lists every visible series at the nearest x; a series with no row at that x reads \"No observation\", distinct from \"No data\". The tooltip stays inside the viewport, does not cover the active mark or any control, can itself be hovered, and lists at most eight rows plus \"+N more\". In a plot too small for it (decision 0004: narrower than 240 px or shorter than 140 px) the same content appears as text in a strip reserved under the plot. Escape closes it until the pointer reaches a different datum. | Hover at 20 positions including all four edges; sparse-series fixture; narrow tile with eight series; Escape test | R15 |\n   125\t| I2 | Legend entries are toggle buttons with a pressed state, operable by click, Enter and Space. | Keyboard and accessibility-tree tests | R12 |\n   126\t| I3 | Zoom on time, date and numeric x axes is reachable four ways: visible Zoom in, Zoom out and Reset buttons that work with single clicks; drag to select a range; `+`, `-`, `0` and Shift+arrows; and pinch when `zoom: 'touch'` is set. The wheel zooms only while the plot has focus, and never when Ctrl or Meta is held, so browser zoom and page scrolling are not intercepted. | Reach a given range by clicks only; by keyboard only; by drag; page scrolls normally with the pointer over an unfocused chart | D7, R12, WCAG 2.5.1, 2.5.7, 1.4.4 |\n   127\t| I4 | Every interaction works with a single pointer without dragging, and by touch. Every control is at least 24×24 CSS px. A one-finger drag on a chart scrolls the page. | Touch emulation; size checks | WCAG 2.5.7, 2.5.8 |\n   128\t| I5 | First render is not animated. An update may transition for at most 200 ms. Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` nothing transitions, on first render or on update. | After `document.fonts.ready`: first frame equals the frame at 2.5 s within a 0.1% pixel tolerance, in both settings; an update under reduced motion reaches its final frame in one step; a 24-chart filter change settles within 200 ms | R14 |\n   129\t| I6 | A chart fed by `append` shows a Pause/Resume control. While paused, new rows are buffered and the view does not move. | Stream test | WCAG 2.2.2 |\n   130\t\n   131\t### 3.4 Accessibility\n   132\t\n   133\tTarget: every WCAG 2.2 level AA success criterion that applies to what Axylo renders, as component-level evidence. Conformance of a page is a property of the page and remains the author's.\n   134\t\n   135\t| ID | Criterion | Verified by | Driven by |\n   136\t|---|---|---|---|\n   137\t| A1 | Every chart has an accessible name: its `title`, or the heading named by `labelledBy`, or else a generated name (\"Line chart of Sessions by Day\") with AX140 raised in every build. The title's heading level is the author's (`level`), and it can be hidden visually. Every chart has a generated summary: type, series, x range with time zone, y range, each series' minimum, maximum and last value, and any omissions. `description` adds to the summary and never removes the zone or omission statements. Element ids are unique per chart. | Accessibility-tree snapshot for every fixture; a 24-chart page has no duplicate ids; axe `heading-order` | R11, R13 |\n   138\t| A2 | Keyboard: at most two tab stops while the table is closed, the plot and one toolbar with roving focus that holds legend toggles, zoom, pause and the table control. Every point is reachable in order; the series can be switched; the ends can be reached directly; focus can leave the chart. The focus indicator is at least 2 px and 3:1 and is not hidden by the tooltip. The exact keys and roles are fixed after the pattern spike in M1 (section 8). | Forward and reverse traversal in collapsed, zoomed, streaming and table-open states; focus after hiding the focused series; indicator contrast | R12 |\n   139\t| A3 | Moving focus to a point conveys its text (series, x, value with unit, position) through the focused element's accessible name or a polite live region. On touch screen readers, every point is reachable by swiping, or the table is reachable within two gestures. | Accessibility-tree snapshot after each key; a recorded rehearsal on NVDA with Chrome, NVDA with Firefox, VoiceOver with Safari on macOS, VoiceOver on iOS, and TalkBack with Chrome | R12, R13 |\n   140\t| A4 | \"View as table\" shows the data as an HTML table built from the normalized data when opened: the title as caption, field labels with units as column headers, x values as row headers, values formatted as in F6. It covers the current x range, 100 rows per page, with every row reachable by paging or by jumping to an x value. It sits in a focusable scroll region no taller than the plot, and opening it does not move other charts. | Table content compared with fixture data, including a value near row 900,000 of 1,000,000; a 24-chart page layout test | R13 |\n   141\t| A5 | Series are never distinguished by color alone, in any mode. Each line and area carries a shape marker at its last point and at sparse intervals, repeated in the legend and tooltip; under `prefers-contrast: more` or forced colors, lines also differ by dash. Adjacent filled marks (slices, stacked segments) are separated by at least 1 px of background. The default palette has eight colors, each at least 3:1 on the default light and dark backgrounds, with a minimum pairwise OKLab difference of 0.10 (provisional) under normal vision and simulated protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. On any other background, Axylo measures the palette against the resolved background and raises AX141 below 3:1. | Palette script scoring the rendered marks of an eight-series chart in both schemes, repeats included; rendered-pixel checks of separators; a grayscale screenshot in which three crossing lines can be told apart by marker | R7, WCAG 1.4.1, 1.4.11 |\n   142\t| A6 | Content reflows at 320 CSS px and 400% zoom without two-dimensional scrolling. User text-spacing overrides do not clip text. | Viewport and style-override tests in three engines | WCAG 1.4.10, 1.4.12 |\n   143\t| A7 | Data arriving does not speak. Announcements happen only for the reader's own navigation, and for a change of state (L7). While data streams, keyboard focus stays on the same datum until it leaves the window. | Stream test counting live-region changes with and without focus; 24 concurrent streams | R12 |\n   144\t| A8 | axe-core reports no violations on any fixture in any state, including `heading-order` and `scrollable-region-focusable`. | CI | R11 |\n   145\t| A9 | A conformance table lists every applicable WCAG 2.2 AA success criterion, the test that covers it, and what the author must supply (a meaningful title or `labelledBy`, series names, units, the page's own structure). It also states the limits in section 3.8. | Published with each release; a CI check that every listed test exists | R11 |\n   146\t| A10 | Every built-in string can be replaced through `messages`. Built-in English text is marked `lang=\"en\"` when the document language is not English. | Test on a `lang=\"de\"` page | WCAG 3.1.2 |\n   147\t\n   148\t### 3.5 Diagnostic registry\n   149\t\n   150\tLevel decides delivery. **Error**: the chart or a series cannot be drawn; the chart shows its error state. **Warning**: something is not drawn as given; the reader sees the note in F12. **Hint**: advice for the author. Errors and warnings print once per code per page in every build; hints print in development builds only. `strict: true` throws on errors and warnings found while validating a create, `update` or `append` call, synchronously from that call. A diagnostic that can only arise later (a contrast check after the page's CSS changes, a custom formatter that throws when a table page is built, a label that stops fitting after a resize) is reported when it is found and is never thrown. Every diagnostic names the chart; those about data name the field and the first row indexes in the caller's own data.\n   151\t\n   152\t| Code | Level | Condition | What is drawn |\n   153\t|---|---|---|---|\n   154\t| AX100 | Error | Typed columns have different lengths | Error state; the message names the columns and their lengths |\n   155\t| AX101 | Error | A named field is not a key of any row | Error state; the message lists the keys that exist and the closest match |\n   156\t| AX102 | Warning | A field is absent (`undefined`) in some rows | Gaps |\n   157\t| AX103 | Warning | A value is `NaN` or infinite | Gap |\n   158\t| AX104 | Hint | Every non-missing value of a value field is a plain decimal string (`'40'`, `'-1.5'`) | Parsed and drawn; the message suggests `parse: 'number'`. An empty string counts as missing |\n   159\t| AX105 | Hint | Steps are absent on a regular time, date, wall-clock or number axis | Gaps. When a series would need more absent steps than twice its observations (and more than 1,000), it is treated as irregular instead: no gaps are created and the hint says so |\n   160\t| AX106 | Warning | A value field mixes numbers with strings, or holds strings that are not plain decimals (`'1,234'`, `'n/a'`) | The strings are not drawn |\n   161\t| AX107 | Warning | A date or time cannot be parsed | That row is not drawn |\n   162\t| AX108 | Error | Duplicate x within a series, or duplicate donut labels | That series, or the donut, is not drawn |\n   163\t| AX109 | Hint | Numbers on an axis declared `time` look like seconds, or a numeric x looks like epoch milliseconds without `type: 'time'` | As declared |\n   164\t| AX110 | Warning | An author domain on bar or area excluded zero | Domain widened to zero |\n   165\t| AX111 | Hint | Instants look like calendar dates | As instants, zone shown |\n   166\t| AX112 | Hint | Date-time strings have no offset | As written |\n   167\t| AX120 | Error | Negative donut value | Error state |\n   168\t| AX121 | Warning | More than eight donut slices | Seven largest plus \"Other (n)\" |\n   169\t| AX130 | Warning | More than eight series | All series, with dash or marker differences |\n   170\t| AX140 | Warning | No `title` and no `labelledBy` | Generated name |\n   171\t| AX141 | Warning | Palette below 3:1 on the resolved background | As themed |\n   172\t| AX142 | Hint | Plot too small to draw | Summary and table control |\n   173\t| AX143 | Hint | Labels hidden after every remedy | Note shown to the reader |\n   174\t| AX150 | Warning | Unknown option key | Ignored; the message suggests the closest known key |\n   175\t| AX151 | Warning | `append` rows out of order | Accepted through the slower full update |\n   176\t| AX131 | Hint | A compact chart has more than one series | Drawn, with dash differences |\n   177\t| AX132 | Hint | More bars than pixels along the category axis | Drawn; the message suggests aggregating |\n   178\t| AX133 | Hint | A scatter chart has more than 50,000 points | Drawn; the message says drawing may be slow |\n   179\t| AX134 | Error | Series × x positions exceeds 20,000,000 (long rows with many series and little shared x) | Error state; the message gives both counts and suggests fewer series or a scatter chart |\n   180\t| AX152 | Warning | `timeZone` is not a zone the browser knows | The viewer's zone is used |\n   181\t| AX160 | Warning | A custom formatter threw | The default format is used for that value |\n   182\t| AX199 | Error | Axylo itself failed while building the chart | Error state with a generic message; the error is passed to `onDiagnostic` and printed |\n   183\t\n   184\tExpected results for the Phase 1 fixtures: the combined `dirty` fixture (`[10, 20, null, NaN, '40', undefined, 70]`) yields AX102, AX103 and AX106 once each, draws Mon–Tue as a segment and Sun as a point, and shows the F12 note. `dirty-string` (one `'40'` among numbers) yields AX106. A column made only of numeric strings yields AX104 and is drawn in full. `dirty-null` yields nothing.\n   185\t\n   186\tThe split between AX104 and AX106 answers a reviewer's objection that common back ends return counts as strings (Postgres `bigint` and `numeric`, BigQuery): a whole column of plain decimal strings is unambiguous and is parsed; a stray string among numbers is a bug and is not.\n   187\t\n   188\t### 3.6 Type matrix\n   189\t\n   190\t| | Line | Area | Bar | Donut | Scatter |\n   191\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   192\t| Picking by pointer | Nearest x | Nearest x | The band under the pointer | The slice under the pointer | Nearest point within 24 px; ties go to the later row |\n   193\t| Tooltip content | Every visible series at that x | Same, plus the stack total | Every series in that category | Label, value, percentage | The point's series, x and y; coincident points listed, up to eight |\n   194\t| Keyboard order | By x, then series | By x, then series | By category, then series | By slice order | By x, then y |\n   195\t| Zoom | On time, date and numeric x only | On time, date and numeric x only | On time, date and numeric x only | No | Yes, both axes later; x only in 1.0 |\n   196\t| Simplified drawing when dense | F5 | F5 on cumulative sums | No; more bars than pixels raises a hint | No | No in 1.0; above 50,000 points a hint says drawing may be slow |\n   197\t| Limit that raises a diagnostic | Eight series | Eight series | Eight series | Eight slices | Eight series |\n   198\t| Reference lines and bands | Yes; included in the domain; listed in the summary and table caption | Yes | Yes | No | Yes |\n   199\t\n   200\t### 3.7 Compact variant\n   201\t\n   202\t`compact: true` on line, area and bar draws the marks and nothing else: no axes, gridlines, legend, toolbar, table control, zoom or tooltip. It is for a small tile where the page already shows the number and the label.\n   203\t\n   204\t| ID | Criterion | Verified by |\n   205\t|---|---|---|\n   206\t| C1 | A compact chart is a static image with a full text alternative: `role=\"img\"`, an accessible name (as in A1, including AX140 when none is given) and the generated summary as its description (series, x range, minimum, maximum, last value, omissions). It has no tab stop and no pointer-only behavior, so nothing is available to a mouse that is not available to a keyboard. | Accessibility-tree snapshot; a page of 40 has zero added tab stops |\n   207\t| C2 | The fidelity rules still hold: zero baseline for bar and area (F1), gaps (F2), diagnostics (F3), simplified drawing (F5), sorting (F11), no motion (I5), scheme from the page (L4). | The same fixtures as the full charts |\n   208\t| C3 | It fills its container at any size from 24×16 CSS px up; with no definite height it is 32 px tall. | Size tests |\n   209\t| C4 | With more than one series, lines differ by dash as well as color, since there is no legend; AX131 suggests one series per compact chart. | Two-series fixture |\n   210\t| C5 | When values were left out (F12), the description says so and a small marker with a text equivalent appears in the corner. | `dirty` fixture in compact mode |\n   211\t\n   212\tA compact chart does not give access to every value; the summary is its alternative. An author who needs every value reachable uses the full chart.\n   107\t### 1.5 Handle and commit contract\n   108\t\n   109\t```ts\n   110\tchart.update({ title: 'Sessions' });                 // options\n   111\tchart.append([{ day: '2026-05-01', channel: 'Direct', sessions: 41210 }], { keep: 120 });   // rows\n   112\tchart.zoom(['2026-03-01', '2026-03-31']);            // view\n   113\tconst off = chart.on('hover', point => { … });\n   114\tchart.diagnostics;                                   // current, as soon as any call returns\n   115\tchart.destroy();\n   116\t```\n   117\t\n   118\tFinding D3: the ten libraries have seven update idioms. Axylo has three methods, one per kind of change, with one contract.\n   119\t\n   120\t| Rule | Detail |\n   121\t|---|---|\n   122\t| Order | Calls are applied in the order made. `update({ data })` followed by `append` appends to the new data. |\n   123\t| Two phases | Each call validates and normalizes synchronously: diagnostics are current when it returns, and a `strict` chart throws from that call. Drawing is deferred to the next animation frame, and calls made before that frame are drawn once. |\n   124\t| Atomic switch | Marks, labels, hit testing and the accessibility layer move to a new data revision together. No frame mixes two revisions. |\n   125\t| Patches | A key present in an `update` replaces the old value whole; a key set to `undefined` returns to its default; absent keys stay. No deep merging. |\n   126\t| Rejected changes | A call that throws under `strict` leaves the chart on its last valid state. |\n   127\t| Streaming | `keep` is the number of distinct x values retained. Rows before the last x are accepted through the slower full update and raise AX151. While zoomed to the latest edge the view follows new data; zoomed elsewhere, it stays put. Paused charts buffer (I6). Keyboard focus stays on its datum until that datum leaves the window (A7). |\n   128\t| Teardown | `destroy()` cancels the pending frame, disconnects observers and listeners, and makes later calls no-ops. |\n   129\t\n   130\t### 1.6 Diagnostics\n   131\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"for p in reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core{4,5,6,7}.fix.report.md; do sed -n '1,140p' \\\"\"'$p\"; done'","aggregated_output":"<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a1d73b9f46c46814f, resumed. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Chart core, fourth fix pass: report\n\nNothing is committed. I stopped at an item boundary. The library type-checks for my files. The one remaining type-check error and the Node acceptance failures are in files that other agents were editing during my runs (see \"Runs\").\n\n### Your three corrections\n1. **The `lang` change no longer fires the theme watcher.** `src/theme/watch.ts` is back to `['class','style','data-theme']`. `lang` is now watched by its own observer, `watchLanguage` in `core/environment.ts`, wired in `core/chart.ts`. It calls `invalidate.language()`, which schedules a frame. `test/browser/render/theme.browser.test.ts` is unedited (`git diff` is empty) and passes 18/18. The language watcher has no browser test of its own yet.\n2. **C4 compact bar: what the group would need.** The test reads only elements whose inline `color` is `var(--axylo-series-color-N)`. In SVG that is the series `<g>`, which has fill `currentColor`. The pattern sits on the overlay child `<rect>`s, which carry no colour style. So both series read `none||` and come out equal.\n   - The cleanest fix in `src/render/svg.ts` `updateBars`: also set `style=\"color: var(--axylo-series-color-N)\"` on the overlay rects (the ones with `fill: url(#axylo-pattern-…)`). The second series then reads `none||pattern`, and nothing changes visually because the pattern's content takes its colour from the `<pattern>` element.\n   - Putting `fill=\"url(#…)\"` on the `<g>` would also pass, but it would be an attribute the CSS overrides, which misdescribes the drawing.\n   - The test's reading is reasonable but tied to SVG.\n3. **L1 at 200% text, 240 px.** The visible first sentence of the summary now wraps (`overflow-wrap: anywhere`, no `nowrap`). The L1 tests pass in the browser acceptance runs.\n\n### Controller review\n| # | Fixed | Test (failed before the fix; \"old\" means the d49e8a8 bundle or tree) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 5 | Re-encoding while paused redraws the displayed rows with the new fields and keeps held rows buffered until Resume | `test/core/snapshot.test.ts` \"pass 4: findings 5 and 8\" |\n| 8 | A valid append clears a stale AX101 (all five types) | same |\n| 12 | Small option objects are copied when accepted (borrowed `data` is not). A label- or unit-only change renames without renormalizing | `snapshot.test.ts` \"finding 12\"; `options.test.ts` |\n| 13 | The AX160 bucket is emptied before formatters are built (so construction-time AX160 survives) and kept while they live. Same code and field are deduplicated. The layout bucket is cleared when no axes are drawn | 4 tests \"finding 13\"; all 4 failed on the old controller |\n| 11 | A title update on a stream no longer walks the retained rows. Summary statistics are reused when only naming inputs change | 2 tests \"finding 11\"; both failed first. Formatter closures not capturing the table: checked by reading only. The buffer copy on append belongs to the data module |\n| 17 (rescoped) | `zoom()` on a category axis or a donut is a no-op reported as AX150 (`field: 'zoom'`). A window kept from a numeric axis never reaches categories | line, area, bar and donut tests \"finding 17\". My partial category-zoom code (band offset, layout offset, whole-category steps) was removed with `git checkout` of my own files |\n| F7 below 200 px | New `coarserDomains` in `scale/domain.ts`. Layout's `ValueAxis.coarser` makes `computeLayout` retry with the first wider domain whose tick set fits whole. Core supplies the candidates. The extent is cached per view and is in the layout key | `test/core/ticks.test.ts` heights 100–700 (failed at 192 px before); `test/scale/domain.test.ts`; `test/layout/layout.test.ts` |\n| 20 (weak tests) | Re-entrancy test now runs its nested update. Dense-line test checks the drawn path. Browser crossing test checks series-colour pixels. `plotRole` test uses an override. A teardown test counts listeners through the DevTools protocol. A late-setup-failure test asserts a frame was requested before the failure | `controller.test.ts`, `review.browser.test.ts`, `lifecycle.browser.test.ts` |\n\n### Documentation author's items\n1. **AX108 on the only series** now shows an error state whose message is the series-not-drawn sentence. The summary follows the state, and the table is offered.\n2. **Event values match what `zoom()` accepts.** `positionValue` returns:\n   - a Date for time axes;\n   - `'YYYY-MM-DD'` for a date at midnight, otherwise the number (a padded bar end; `zoom()` reads it as the same position);\n   - the shortest offset-free ISO string for wall-clock axes;\n   - the category name, otherwise the number.\n\n   I also fixed a bug this exposed: a wall-clock window on a wall-clock axis was rejected because its AX112 hint counted as an error. Hints no longer reject a window, and that AX112 is dropped for wall axes. Round-trip tests pass for all four axis kinds. Sentence for `public.ts` on the zoom event and `Point.x`: \"In the form `zoom()` accepts for this axis (a Date for instants, 'YYYY-MM-DD' for dates, an ISO date-time without offset for wall-clock times, the category, else the number), so it can be passed to another chart's `zoom()` unchanged.\"\n3. **Loading and error summaries are now the state text**, no longer \"No data to show.\".\n4. **Donut percentages: no change.** The legend, tooltip, table and summary all use `formatters.percent`, so the tooltip shows six digits too. Spec F6 gives readouts six significant fraction digits, and F8 gives shares no rule. If one fraction digit is wanted, F8 needs a sentence, and the change is in `src/format`.\n\n### Reader review, finding 5\nThe reader has no exported sentence builder yet, so there is a marked call site in `controller.ts`. The stand-in follows the reader's `{seeTable}` rule; its shape is `seriesNotDrawnSentence(messages: Messages, series: string, table: boolean): string`. The note language now counts `seeTable` when the note's templates contain it. `FigureModel.noteSegments: {text, lang}[]` exists and `figure.ts` renders each run as a `<span lang>`. For now the controller passes one segment; the reader's per-run segments plug into that call site. One case stays wrong until then: an overridden template containing the built-in \"See table.\" is not tagged. Tests are in `snapshot.test.ts` \"reader review finding 5\".\n\n### Interaction review\n| Item | Fixed | Test (`test/browser/chart/review4.browser.test.ts`; all failed on the old bundle except where noted) |\n|---|---|---|\n| new 7 | `zoomStep` makes zoom-in strictly narrower and zoom-out strictly wider for keys, wheel and buttons | browser test, plus `focus2.test.ts` property and the reviewer's [40,45] case |\n| new 8 | Zoom controls and recovery are only offered for a real empty window. The plot reads the state text (\"Loading chart.\"). With every series hidden the range is 0/\"No data to show.\" and the legend still recovers | 2 tests |\n| new 6 | The overlay is cleared before the frame is dropped. Input state is reset. Focus goes to the table control, or to the figure (`tabindex=-1`, no new tab stop) | 2 tests |\n| new 10 | A pinch is bound to its two pointer ids. Cancel, blur, detach and rebuild drop the queued frame; a normal lift applies the last move. Mouse presses are always captured | pinch-cancel test fails on old. The release-outside test passes on old as well, so it is a guard only |\n| part 1 #2 | Pins and dismissals map by exact category; keyboard focus still moves to the successor | 2 tests (append with `keep`) |\n| part 1 #10 | same as new 10 | |\n| part 3, `focus2.test.ts:68` | Now starts from a known representable narrowing and asserts that zooming in is exhausted | |\n\n**Not done:** new item 9 (touch-sized row and slice actions); part 1 items 3 (not re-checked), 9 (minimum window not changed beyond the direction rule), 11, 12, 13 with decision 0004 rule 4, and 15; part 3's other weak tests.\n\n### Edits outside `src/core` and `src/dom`\n- `src/theme/watch.ts`: attribute list reverted (no test needed; the render theme test covers it).\n- `src/scale/domain.ts`, `src/scale/index.ts`: `coarserDomains`, tested in `test/scale/domain.test.ts`.\n- `src/layout/index.ts`, `src/layout/labels.ts`: `ValueAxis.coarser`, `FittedLabels.partial`, and the retry. Tested in `test/layout/layout.test.ts`.\n  - The layout author edited these same files and the test file at the same time; their code sits in the working tree beside mine.\n  - Once, for about ten seconds, I wrote the HEAD versions of `index.ts` and `labels.ts` and then restored my copy. Their edits are visible on top of mine afterwards, but ask them to check nothing was lost.\n- `src/theme/css.ts` (figure section).\n- `test/core/host.ts`: new `pageLang` option. Someone else also added `timeZone`, `locale`, `textWidth` and `captionLineHeight` there, and changed `src/index.ts` imports to `./public.js`.\n- **Shared bundle:** to show tests fail on the old code, I swapped `dist` to the d49e8a8 bundle several times and rebuilt afterwards. Other agents' browser runs in that window may have used the old bundle.\n\n### How to run acceptance on canvas\nDon't. The suite reads the SVG DOM. My renderer switch in `test/browser/chart/util.ts` now applies only to tests under `test/browser/(chart|a11y)/`, so `AXYLO_RENDERER=canvas` no longer reaches acceptance. Canvas is covered by my two directories.\n\n### Runs (last lines)\n- **Type check:** exit 1. The one error is `packages/axylo/test/acceptance/dx-diagnostics.test.ts(180,9) TS2322`, a file the acceptance agent was editing. An earlier run also showed an error in `src/reader/table.ts`, also edited by another agent.\n- **`npm test`:** `Test Files 13 failed | 62 passed (75)`, `Tests 83 failed | 2122 passed (2205)`. Every failure is in `test/acceptance`: 8 of the 13 files are `.scratch/` mutation runs, and the rest are files being edited. The same f-domains, f-donut, f-format, dx-diagnostics, f-stacks and dx-controller tests also fail against the HEAD tree.\n- **Node core, scale and layout:** `Test Files 18 passed (18)`, `Tests 284 passed (284)`.\n- **Browser, my directories, SVG:** `Test Files 12 passed (12)`, `Tests 174 passed (174)`.\n- **Browser, my directories, canvas:** `Test Files 12 passed (12)`, `Tests 174 passed (174)`.\n- **Browser acceptance, SVG:** `Test Files 4 failed | 9 passed (13)`, `Tests 14 failed | 455 passed (469)`. That run overlapped my bundle swaps and the suite's own edits. On a stable bundle the failing set is 9 tests (A7 bar sliding window, A10 bar, A2 focus indicators ×5, C4 compact bar, T-tooltip-donut), and the same 9 fail against the HEAD bundle.\n  - One real regression of mine, I3 bar (date `positionValue` dropping a padded end), is fixed and the I3 tests pass 20/20.\n  - I did not re-run the full acceptance suite after the last reader-sentence changes; my own directories were re-run on that final build.\n\nLogs are in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-canarit--claude-spares-spare-6ClT4i/23402a37-81bb-469c-a14a-8bf7f048d066/scratchpad/core-fix/` (`p7-svg.txt`, `p7-canvas.txt`, `p6-acc-svg.txt`, `p7-npmtest.txt`, `p7-tsc.txt`).\n\n### Contract changes\nNone needed.\n\n<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a1d73b9f46c46814f, resumed. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Chart core, fifth pass: report\n\nNothing is committed and the tree compiles. Everything you listed is done except interaction item 13 with decision 0004 rule 4 (the readout's reserved space) and part of the part-3 weak-test list; both are explained under \"Not done\". I did not touch the shared `dist` to test old code: the old revision (88a8b96) is built privately at `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-canarit--claude-spares-spare-6ClT4i/23402a37-81bb-469c-a14a-8bf7f048d066/scratchpad/core-fix/old5/`. A new switch in `test/browser/chart/util.ts`, `AXYLO_BUNDLE=<dir>`, loads that bundle into pages of my own suites only.\n\n### 1. F7: the domain ends at the first drawn tick at or beyond each extreme\n- **Cause:** a floating-point comparison in `core/axes.ts` `endingCandidates`. The check `b - step < hi` let the 0.1-step tick set through, because 0.2 − 0.1000…09 comes out just below 0.1.\n- **Fix:** each tick set is now checked on its own tick values. The first tick at or above the maximum must be the last tick, and the last tick at or below the minimum must be the first. `scale/domain.ts` was already exact.\n- **Tests:**\n  - `test/core/axes.test.ts`: the [-0.8, 0.2] case (failed before the fix) and a property test.\n  - `test/scale/domain.test.ts`: property \"an extreme equal to k × step ends the domain there\".\n  - `f-domains.test.ts`: 28/28 pass.\n\n### 2. Donut shares: at most one fraction digit\n- A new `shareText` in `format/number.ts` is what `formatters.percent` now uses. It rounds the exact decimal, so 0.1235 reads 12.4%.\n- Values on a percent or ratio scale keep their F6 readout digits.\n- Tests in `test/format/index.test.ts`: 17.2%, the German form, 12.4%, 33.3%, and a ratio value that stays 17.241379%.\n\n### C4: the series colour on the pattern overlay\n- `render/svg.ts` `updateBars`: the overlay rects that carry the pattern also carry the series colour style. The colour is part of the cache key, so a theme change updates it.\n- Test in `test/browser/render/review.browser.test.ts`: the elements carrying the series colour whose fill is a pattern. It failed before the fix and passes now; the render suite is 84 passed, 1 skipped.\n\n### 3. Interaction review\n| Item | What changed | Old bundle |\n|---|---|---|\n| new 9 | Choosable tooltip rows and every donut slice-list entry (zero and null slices included) are buttons named by their text, with `tabindex=-1`, so the closed chart still has two tab stops. Clicking a slice entry selects it; the press does not move focus. Opening the table by keyboard closes a pin (this already worked). | 2 of 3 tests fail on old; the pin test passes on old and stays as a guard |\n| part 1 item 3 | All-zero donut with `table: false` still lists its slices. Already worked. | passes on old (guard) |\n| part 1 item 9 | `minimumWidth` is now at most half the axis and at least one unit in the last place: two or three positions over [0,100] can be halved, and [1e16, 1e16+4] halves to a width of 2. | Node tests in `focus2.test.ts` failed before the fix |\n| part 1 item 11 | A pinned scatter point is dropped when its point has no drawn anchor. Otherwise the group is rebuilt by picking at that anchor, so new coincident points are counted. | both tests fail on old |\n| part 1 item 12 | `core/chart.ts` `measure()` now gives layout pixels rather than transformed viewport pixels. One conversion (`cssScale` in `tooltip.ts`) is used for picking, anchors, tooltip size and placement, and the readout. Ratios within 2% are treated as offsetWidth's integer rounding, not as a transform. | fails on old |\n| part 1 item 15 | An open table and its control stay inside the card when the card shrinks and text doubles. Already worked: no inline heights. | passes on old (guard) |\n| language watcher | Changing `lang` on the document changes number formatting to `1.234,5`, marks built-in text `lang=\"en\"`, and runs no theme stage. | passes on old (guard) |\n\nThe new tests are in `test/browser/chart/review5.browser.test.ts`.\n\n**24 px rows trade-off (decision for you):**\n- With 24 px rows everywhere, the hover tooltip grew about 12 px. At two plot edges it then no longer fit beside the mark, so the existing test \"at each of the four plot edges…\" fell back to the readout and failed.\n- What I did: rows are 24 px when the tooltip is pinned by a tap, in the fixed readout, and in the slice list. A mouse-hover tooltip keeps text-height rows, which are still buttons.\n- So WCAG 2.5.8 is met wherever rows are acted on by touch. It is not met for mouse clicks on hover rows. If you want 24 px rows there too, tell me and I will change the edge test's fixture instead.\n\n### 4. Tests that passed with the behaviour broken\n- Click test (`review2`): now asserts the floating tooltip's title and the exact selected x at each of the four positions.\n- Contrast dash test: no longer skips when every plotted SVG path is solid.\n- Donut legend: a second fixture where value and share differ, expecting \"3 (60%)\" and \"2 (40%)\".\n- Zoom exclusions: now covers category bar, line, area and donut, by buttons and the `+` key.\n- Coarse-double loop in `focus2` (pass 4).\n\nExpectations I changed because the requirement changed: \"two or three positions cannot be zoomed\" (focus2 and review2) became the attainable-minimum rule; \"the legend has no buttons\" became buttons outside the tab order; the note runs in `snapshot.test.ts` are now per run.\n\n### 5. Reader helper, note runs and AX143\n- The stand-in is gone; the call site imports `seriesNotDrawnSentence` from `../reader`.\n- `FigureModel.noteSegments` takes the reader's runs. A run is marked `en` only on a page in another language.\n- Node test: overriding only `seeTable` leaves \"Siehe Tabelle.\" unmarked; overriding only the sentence marks the built-in \"See table.\" `en`.\n- `figure.ts` no longer adds spaces between runs; the reader's runs carry their own.\n- AX143 now passes `chartType`, `xKind` (taken from the frame for scatter as well) and `horizontal` for bars. Node test: vertical category bars get the horizontal-bar hint, a category line does not.\n\n### 6. Mixed-sign totals\n`focus.ts` already takes the total text from the lookup's tooltip model and computes no net. A Node test checks a stack of +3 and −2: the tooltip total is \"3 and -2\" and the focused text contains \"Total 3 and -2\".\n\nNone of my tests depend on worker threads, so the switch to forked processes changes nothing for them.\n\n### Edits outside `src/core` and `src/dom`\n- `src/render/svg.ts`: the C4 change only.\n- `src/format/number.ts` and `src/format/index.ts`: share precision only.\n- `src/theme/css.ts`: the figure section (choice buttons).\n- Test files: `test/scale/domain.test.ts`, `test/format/index.test.ts`, `test/browser/render/review.browser.test.ts`.\n\n### Not done\n- **Item 13 with rule 4 (reserved space for the readout).** Reserving space when the floating tooltip might not fit costs a small tile's plot room on every chart; that is why I reverted it in pass 3. Placing the readout inside the plot column stops it covering the controls but drops \"reserved\". I need a decision: reserve space only below some figure width (which width?), or allow the readout over the plot.\n- **Part 3, remaining:**\n  - the 40-move sweep at several strides;\n  - a clipped fallback that passes `isVisible()`;\n  - the native-range and narrowed-scatter adjustments;\n  - selecting a secondary row by touch in the readout (the pinned-tooltip case is covered);\n  - the area-marker oracle;\n  - the speech-related tests (screen-reader output cannot be observed here).\n\n### Runs (last lines)\n- **Type check:** exit 0.\n- **`npx vitest run packages/axylo/test --exclude '**/acceptance/**'`:** `Test Files 2 failed | 43 passed (45)`, `Tests 2 failed | 768 passed (770)`.\n  - `data/streaming-storage.test.ts` \"bounds the retained typed-array backing…\": data module, under edit.\n  - `simplify.test.ts` \"million-slot outlier\": a timing limit (38 ms against 30) under load; it passes when run alone.\n- **Browser chart and a11y, SVG:** `Test Files 13 passed (13)`, `Tests 184 passed (184)`.\n- **Browser chart and a11y, canvas:** `Test Files 13 passed (13)`, `Tests 184 passed (184)`.\n- **Browser render:** `Test Files 5 passed | 1 skipped (6)`, `Tests 84 passed | 1 skipped (85)`.\n- **`npx vitest run packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts`:** `Test Files 1 passed (1)`, `Tests 28 passed (28)`.\n\nLogs are `p9-*.txt` in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-canarit--claude-spares-spare-6ClT4i/23402a37-81bb-469c-a14a-8bf7f048d066/scratchpad/core-fix/`.\n\nNo contract changes needed.\n\n<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a1d73b9f46c46814f, resumed. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Chart core, sixth pass: report\n\nNothing is committed. The browser acceptance suite (SVG) is at 538 of 551, up from 899/37 failures across all suites at d8b4150. The 13 that still fail are three groups: a test-procedure limit, a conflict between the decision's geometry and the test path, and a browser timing limit. Each is explained below with a suggested way out. I did not swap the shared `dist`: old-code checks used the privately built 0e5aa29 bundle through my `AXYLO_BUNDLE` switch.\n\n### Decision 0004 revision 2, implemented as written\n- **`src/dom/tooltip.ts`, rewritten.**\n  - **Placement:** the position comes from the datum alone: the box of its active marks, enlarged by the ring's reach (`RING_REACH` = 9 px).\n  - **Candidates:** above, below, right, left; horizontal bars right, left, above, below; donut tries the hole first. A candidate is valid only wholly inside the plot rectangle (inset 4 px, clear of the plot outline), the viewport and every clipping ancestor, overlapping neither the box nor any control of the figure.\n  - **Rule 6:** rows are dropped into \"+N more\"; if nothing is valid with one row, the candidate that overlaps the box least is used, inside the plot.\n  - **Hovered vs pinned:** a hovered tooltip has `pointer-events: none` and text rows; a pinned one takes events and its rows are buttons of at least 24 × 24 px.\n  - **`strip()`:** running text \"x: series value; …; +N more\" fitted to two lines; entries become 24 px buttons when pinned.\n- **`src/dom/interaction.ts`.**\n  - **Pinning:** a click pins, as a tap already did. A pinned tooltip ignores moves until Escape, a click elsewhere, a keyboard move, or its datum leaving.\n  - **Holding on scatter and donut:** the datum is held while the pointer is inside the rectangle its tooltip had (computed in the plot's own move handler).\n  - **Readout mode:** a class on the figure; the strip and the axis area under the plot count as hoverable.\n- **`src/core/controller.ts`, readout mode by layout.** The plot rectangle without the strip, laid out in the plot's whole column (`room`, from `chart.ts` `measure()`), is under 240 × 140. One more condition: the plot must keep the L8 minimum of 80 px beside the strip.\n  - Without that condition, the 24 tiles of 340 × 200 in I5 fell into the too-small fallback and drew nothing.\n  - With it, L8 by height and I5 both pass.\n  - The decision does not depend on the strip, so it does not oscillate.\n- **Figure and CSS:** the readout element now sits in the plot's column under the plot (`figure.ts`). The strip is two reserved lines (`css.ts`, figure section).\n- **Rings are drawn inside the plot's box** (`core/focus.ts` `buildOverlay`), so the ring at the last point and at the top of a donut is painted. The A2 focus-indicator tests pass.\n\n### Other items\n- **A7 bar:** the category remap now remaps the text's own datum too, so a sliding window no longer rewrites it. New test fails on 0e5aa29 and passes now.\n- **JSON in the page:** the source was `note.dataset.segments = JSON.stringify(runs)` in `figure.ts`. That comparison is now kept in memory. The distribution browser run passes (30/30).\n- **L1 late font:** the cause was that `FontFace.load()` followed by `document.fonts.add()` never fires `loadingdone`. A font probe in the text layer is watched with a ResizeObserver; when it changes size, the fonts are invalidated and everything is laid out again (`chart.ts`, `css.ts`). The L1 late-font tests pass.\n- **L8 short summary:** first sentence, at most two lines, ellipsis beyond (line clamp in `css.ts`). L8 tests pass.\n- **L4:** theme changes are now resolved and written inside the observer's callback, with the canvas still repainted once through the scheduler. The class, style and data-theme triggers pass on all six kinds.\n- **Wiring from the scene and lookup author:**\n  - `buildLookup` gets the device pixel ratio, and on scatter it is in the lookup's cache key.\n  - The donut focus outline uses `donutGeometry`'s adjusted angles.\n  - T-pointer-scatter and T-dense-donut pass.\n- **Item 5:** the reader's `seriesNotDrawnSentence` and runs were wired in pass 5 and still are. **AX143** passes `chartType`, `xKind` and `horizontal`.\n- **Item 6:** `focus.ts` takes the total from the lookup's tooltip model and computes no net total.\n\n### Still failing (13), and why\n1. **I1 \"readout mode … 139 px high\", 5 types.** Entering readout mode reserves the strip, so the plot jumps from about 140 px straight to about 92 px; no plot height exists in between. The test's bisection (`plotTo`) stops on whichever side it probed last, and here it is the 140.07 px side. At 139 px the library is in readout mode. The width bracket passes. This needs a test change: for example, report the last readout-side height of the bisection.\n2. **I1 bar hover.** The fixture's bars reach within about 40 px of the plot top, so neither \"above\" nor \"below\" fits. The tooltip goes beside the box, and the straight path crosses into the next band at step 1 (\"rows changed\"). Under rule 3 only an approach across the reading axis keeps the datum.\n3. **I1 donut hover.** \"Hole first\" puts the tooltip in the hole. The straight path from the Travel slice crosses the Rent slice (steps 10–18) and the empty hole before entering the rectangle. The tooltip shown last on the way was Rent's, which is narrower, so at step 24 the pointer is outside Rent's rectangle and nothing is held. Rule 3 holds a datum only inside its tooltip's rectangle.\n4. **L4, 6 kinds: only the `prefers-color-scheme` part fails.** Probe: after `emulateMedia({colorScheme:'dark'})`, `matchMedia(...).matches` is already true in the next rAF, but Chrome dispatches the `change` event one frame later. No JavaScript can resolve the theme earlier. A fix for charts with `color-scheme: light dark` would be for theme resolution (`src/theme`, not mine) to write `light-dark(light, dark)` values, which the browser switches by itself. Otherwise the test would need to wait two frames.\n\nFor items 2 and 3 I need your decision: change the test path, or change the decision (for example, no \"hole first\" on donut, or a hold along the path).\n\n### Expectations of my own tests changed for revision 2\nThese now assert the revised rules:\n- **The tooltip's position:**\n  - \"four plot edges\" no longer requires the pointer to be outside the tooltip; it asserts the tooltip does not move while the datum is unchanged.\n  - The scale(2) test checks the tooltip stays inside the plot instead of centred on the bar.\n- **Pinning and rows:**\n  - A click pins; a hovered row is text, and a pinned row is the button that selects.\n  - The hover-event sequence is adjusted for click-pinning.\n  - The coincident-count test accepts rows plus \"+N more\" adding up to nine.\n- **Readout mode:**\n  - The narrow-tile and axe readout tests use a 220 px tile, since readout mode now starts below 240 px.\n  - The readout text may end in \"+N more\".\n\nThere is also a new L4 first-frame test in `test/browser/chart/theme.browser.test.ts`. It passes on old code too, so it is a guard only.\n\n### Edits outside `src/core` and `src/dom`\n- **`src/theme/css.ts`** (figure section only): tooltip, strip, choice buttons, font probe, summary line clamp.\n- **No layout changes.** I tried a `minimum` option in `src/layout` during the pass, then removed it, and `src/layout` and `test/layout` match HEAD. The final full run happened before that removal, with the option present but unused.\n\n### Runs (last lines)\n- **Type check:** exit 0.\n- **`npx vitest run packages/axylo/test --exclude '**/acceptance/**'`:** `Test Files 1 failed | 45 passed (46)`, `Tests 1 failed | 775 passed (776)`. The one failure is the kept memory test in `data/streaming-storage`.\n- **My browser directories, SVG:** `Test Files 13 passed (13)`, `Tests 187 passed (187)`.\n- **My browser directories, canvas:** `Test Files 13 passed (13)`, `Tests 187 passed (187)`.\n- **`AXYLO_BROWSER=1 npx vitest run packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance` (SVG):** `Test Files 2 failed | 11 passed (13)`, `Tests 13 failed | 538 passed (551)`.\n- **`AXYLO_BROWSER=1 npx vitest run --config tests/dist/vitest.config.ts`:** `Test Files 4 passed (4)`, `Tests 30 passed (30)`.\n\nLogs are `r1-*.txt` in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-canarit--claude-spares-spare-6ClT4i/23402a37-81bb-469c-a14a-8bf7f048d066/scratchpad/core-fix/`.\n\n<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a1d73b9f46c46814f, resumed. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Chart core, seventh pass: report\n\nAll five items are done. Browser acceptance on SVG now passes in full, 555 of 555, and both items you asked me to confirm (I5 and L1 bar at 200% text) pass in it. Nothing is committed; I did not swap the shared `dist` (old-code checks used private builds of 4504ca4 via `AXYLO_BUNDLE`).\n\n### 1. Rule 3b: a rest holds the datum along the corridor (`src/dom/interaction.ts`)\n- **Rest:** a pointer that stays within 2 CSS px for 250 ms, measured with the events' own timestamps, has rested.\n- **Where it applies:** when the datum's floating tooltip is not across the reading axis (beside a bar or stack; always on scatter and donut).\n- **Hold:** after a rest, the datum is held while the pointer is inside the convex hull of the resting point and the tooltip's rectangle. Leaving the hull resumes picking on that same move; a pointer that never rested is never held. The tooltip stays pointer-transparent and does not move.\n- **One adjustment:** the corridor opens on the first move after the rest, even a move of 2 px or less. Without that, a datum resting exactly on a band edge (the acceptance bar probe) changed on the first 1 px step.\n- **Tests:** five browser tests in `test/browser/chart/review6.browser.test.ts`:\n  - bar after a rest;\n  - bar without a rest, where the datum changes;\n  - leaving the rectangle away from the corridor;\n  - a fast sweep after a rest elsewhere;\n  - donut with the tooltip in the hole.\n\n  On 4504ca4 the three that need the hold fail; the no-rest and sweep tests also pass on old code, so they only guard.\n\n### 2. L4 on a prefers-color-scheme change, fixed in CSS (`src/theme/`)\n- **Stylesheet (`css.ts`):** the `.axylo` private defaults are now `light-dark(light, dark)`, so they switch in the frame the media query does. Fixed sets remain under `[data-axylo-scheme=\"light\"]` and `[data-axylo-scheme=\"dark\"]`. The comment says `light-dark()` is supported by the current and previous major versions of the four browsers in spec 2.3.\n- **Resolution (`resolve.ts`):** when the chart's computed `color-scheme` is anything but `normal` and no `--axylo-background` decides, no `data-axylo-scheme` is written. The per-series properties were already references, not frozen colours.\n  - With `color-scheme: normal` or `--axylo-background`, it works as before.\n  - Forced colours and `prefers-contrast` are unchanged and still pass in the render suite.\n- **Canvas:** it still repaints when the change event arrives, one frame behind; a comment in `controller.ts` says so, and AX141 is judged then.\n- **Tests:**\n  - `test/theme/review.test.ts` checks the generated stylesheet.\n  - `test/browser/render/scheme.browser.test.ts` emulates the media change under `color-scheme: light dark` and reads the mark colour in the first rAF. It fails on 4504ca4.\n- **Tests changed:** three render tests and two of my chart tests expected the attribute in \"page sets color-scheme\" cases. They now expect none, which is the design change, not a loosened check.\n\n### 3. Two-tone focus ring (palette review B1)\n- **Datum ring (`core/focus.ts`):** a 4 px background-colour surround with the 2 px focus colour on top, i.e. 1 px of background on each side. Corners are closed, the ring is kept inside the plot's box, and the tooltip's avoid-box grows by the surround (`RING_REACH` 10).\n- **Plot outline (`css.ts`):** an inset `box-shadow` in the background colour under the 2 px outline. `forced-color-adjust: none` keeps it in forced colours, where both tokens are already system colours.\n- **Tests:**\n  - New browser test (`review6`): dark scheme, a bar of each of the 8 dark series colours, painted pixels at device pixel ratio 2. Crossing the ring finds background, then focus colour, then background, and the ring really crosses the neighbouring bar. It fails on 4504ca4 and passes on both renderers.\n  - `test/core/focus.test.ts`: its expectation changed from 4 focus rules to 4 surround rules plus 4 focus rules.\n- The acceptance A2 tests still pass.\n\n### 4. Untitled chart named by its target's id (React review C6)\n- `Host.targetId`, from `root.id` in `chart.ts`, is used for the diagnostic chart name and for the internal-error delivery. The allocated id stays for the DOM relationships.\n- Node tests in `snapshot.test.ts`: \"sessions\" when the target has that id, the allocated id otherwise. `test/core/host.ts` has a new `targetId` option.\n\n### Edits outside `src/core` and `src/dom`\n- `src/theme/css.ts`: the token blocks and the ring surround.\n- `src/theme/resolve.ts`: the scheme attribute rule only.\n- `test/theme/review.test.ts`, `test/browser/render/scheme.browser.test.ts` (new), and the expectations in `test/browser/render/theme.browser.test.ts` and `review.browser.test.ts`.\n- `test/browser/chart/util.ts`: `AXYLO_BUNDLE` now also reaches the render suites, without the renderer switch.\n- `palette.ts` and `test/theme/palette.test.ts` show as modified in the tree, but those are the palette author's changes, not mine.\n\n### Runs (last lines, final build)\n- **Type check:** clean.\n  - In the chained run it failed once with `packages/react/src/index.ts(114,50): error TS2554`, while the React author was editing that file.\n  - Re-run afterwards: `tsc -p packages/axylo --noEmit && tsc -p docs/api && tsc -p packages/react && tsc -p tests/dist`, no errors.\n- **Node suite without acceptance:** `Test Files 2 failed | 44 passed (46)`, `Tests 2 failed | 791 passed (793)`. Neither failure is mine:\n  - the kept memory test (`data/streaming-storage`);\n  - `scene/scene.test.ts` \"keeps generated geometry finite and clipped across independent chart states\", which fails identically on a clean HEAD tree (2727a30).\n- **My browser directories, SVG:** `Test Files 14 passed (14)`, `Tests 193 passed (193)`.\n- **My browser directories, canvas:** `Test Files 14 passed (14)`, `Tests 193 passed (193)`.\n- **Render (browser):** `Test Files 6 passed | 1 skipped (7)`, `Tests 86 passed | 1 skipped (87)`.\n- **Theme (Node):** `Test Files 3 passed (3)`, `Tests 52 passed (52)`.\n- **Browser acceptance, SVG:** `Test Files 13 passed (13)`, `Tests 555 passed (555)`.\n\nLogs are `s3-*.txt` in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-canarit--claude-spares-spare-6ClT4i/23402a37-81bb-469c-a14a-8bf7f048d066/scratchpad/core-fix/`.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
