{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show a518cbb:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.controller.review.md | tail -34\nrg -n '\"'^#|''^'\"\\\\*\\\\*|\"'^-'\"' reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show a518cbb:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.controller.review.md | tail -34\nrg -n '\"'^#|''^'\"\\\\*\\\\*|\"'^-'\"' reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core7.fix.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"15. **M · Scatter drops the declared percentage scale when computing the domain. Ran.** Create a scatter with y values `20` and `63` and `y.scale: 'percent'`. The upper bound is `70`, although F7 requires `100`. Tick formatting receives the scale, but the controller’s scatter view state omits it. Pass the resolved value scale into that branch and assert the domain for both `percent` and `ratio`. [Scatter view state](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/stages.ts:67) · [Scatter domain calculation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:329)\n\n16. **M · A zoom at the latest bar or scatter datum can stop following. Ran.** For scatter at x `0` and `9`, zoom to `[5,9]` and append `12`. The window stays `[5,9]`. For continuous bars at `0,5,10`, zoom to `[5,10]` and append `15`. That window also stays put. The controller tests the niced or padded `xFull` edge rather than the newest datum. Plan §1.5 requires the live window to follow the data edge. Determine whether the window follows from the latest data position, then clamp the shifted window to the author’s bounds. [Edge detection](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:205) · [Append follow logic](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:538)\n\n17. **M · Category zoom changes the visible rows without changing the axis. Ran for line and area.** Create categories A–D and call `zoom(['B','C'])`. The view limits picking and rows to B and C, but layout still emits four ticks on a four-band projection and the controller exposes no zoom controls. This leaves the chart’s geometry inconsistent with its visible range under plan §1.5 and the spec §3.6 type matrix. Use the same ordinal window and offset for the projection, ticks, marks and lookup, and enable controls for supported category charts. [Category layout](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:103) · [Zoom controls](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:925)\n\n18. **M · An all-missing bar window suppresses the required missing marks. Ran.** Create bars `A: null` and `B: null`. The table contains both rows, but the controller shows “No data to show” and sends an empty scene. Its readiness check requires a finite value even though the bar scene can draw missing glyphs at the baseline. F2 requires those glyphs. Treat retained missing bar slots as drawable and reserve the empty state for a window with no drawable slots. [Display classification](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:721) · [Drawable-content check](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1368)\n\n19. **M · Environment changes can be missed or cause two draws in one frame. Ran the callback sequences. Reasoned through browser wiring.** After drawing at DPR 1, change the host to DPR 3 and signal reattachment. The committed ratio stays 1 until a separate DPR notification. Reattachment also leaves the font epoch alone, so a font load missed while detached can leave cached widths in use. Changing only the document’s `lang` has no watcher. Conversely, executing the scheduled data update and then the theme watcher’s callback produces two draws in the same frame callback batch. Plan §2.2, F5, F6 and the renderer contract require fresh environment inputs and one mark draw per animation frame. Refresh inputs on reattachment, watch language changes, and feed theme invalidation into the same frame scheduler. [Controller invalidation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1211) · [Reattachment](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:109) · [Theme watcher](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/watch.ts:11)\n\n20. **m · Several regression tests can pass when the behavior named in the test is broken. Reasoned from assertions. Ran the host accessor check.** The Node re-entrancy test receives AX140 before its `chart` variable is assigned, so its nested update never runs. The dense-line test reads indices recomputed by `__bench.describe()`, so it can pass with a broken scene. The browser crossing test checks only that the message is hidden, and the `plotRole` test supplies no role override. The browser teardown test can pass with listeners still registered because the destroyed controller suppresses their effects. The setup-failure test throws before any frame is scheduled. The stand-in’s `Object.assign` also snapshots `pending` and `layout`, so those properties cannot verify frame timing. Assert actual output and listener registration, and exercise the missing sequences directly. Within the scoped files I found no test for a stream receiving appends with **zero** frame callbacks, Resume-to-first-frame row provenance, late setup failure, or two live charts on the same target. [Controller tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/controller.test.ts:170) · [Dense-line test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/controller.test.ts:579) · [Host accessors](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/host.ts:143) · [Browser review tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review.browser.test.ts:175) · [Setup failure test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review.browser.test.ts:316) · [Plot role test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review.browser.test.ts:493) · [Teardown test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/lifecycle.browser.test.ts:285)\n\n## Verification\n\nI reviewed the created, pending-first-frame, drawn, paused, failed and destroyed states across static and streaming instances of all five types. I checked call-time validation and diagnostics separately from frame-time marks, labels and lookup. The stage probes covered data and encoding, field presentation, domains and references, chart variants and visibility, caption and controls, locale and time zone, colors, resize, fonts and DPR. I exercised all 14 stage failure hooks, plus actual throwing host render methods and author callbacks.\n\nThe review was read-only. I loaded the exact commit into memory for the Node probes and ran the core Vitest suite in the thread pool with both caches disabled. The browser tests were inspected only. Browser rendering, native observer behavior and the full P7 heap budget remain unverified. I used the donut label as its `keep` key and read §3.6 as including category zoom for line and area. The proposed fixes fit the existing fixed contracts.\n\n```text\nTest Files  8 passed (8)\n     Tests  86 passed (86)\n  Start at  05:47:13\n  Duration  528ms (transform 63%, tests 19%, import 16%, worker 1%)\n```\n\n## Areas examined and found sound\n\n- **Ordinary call order, ran.** Data replacement, append and applicable zoom before the first frame produced one draw. A subsequent explicit data replacement discarded the stream.\n- **Fresh option patches, ran.** Whole-object replacement restored omitted nested defaults, explicit `undefined` restored the top-level default, and absent keys kept their values.\n- **Static ownership, ran.** Clean, ascending `Float64Array` x and y columns were borrowed for all four Cartesian types in the tested fixtures. Donut borrowed its value column. Appending left the caller’s values unchanged.\n- **Ordinary strict rejection, ran.** A rejected strict create disposed its host before drawing. The ninth-series test preserved the previous data through a later valid append. Invalid strict zoom reported AX107 without throwing or moving the window.\n- **Attached environment and layout caches, ran.** Explicit locale and time-zone changes reached the formatter, font notifications invalidated measurements, and data replacement with unchanged tick inputs reused layout.\n- **Ordinary destruction and callback exceptions, ran.** Repeated destroy disposed once, canceled the first frame, and made later calls inert. Throwing author handlers left the chart usable.\n- **Registry coverage, reasoned.** Every §3.5 code has an emission path, and I found no emitted AX code outside the registry.3:## Chart core, seventh pass: report\n7:### 1. Rule 3b: a rest holds the datum along the corridor (`src/dom/interaction.ts`)\n8:- **Rest:** a pointer that stays within 2 CSS px for 250 ms, measured with the events' own timestamps, has rested.\n9:- **Where it applies:** when the datum's floating tooltip is not across the reading axis (beside a bar or stack; always on scatter and donut).\n10:- **Hold:** after a rest, the datum is held while the pointer is inside the convex hull of the resting point and the tooltip's rectangle. Leaving the hull resumes picking on that same move; a pointer that never rested is never held. The tooltip stays pointer-transparent and does not move.\n11:- **One adjustment:** the corridor opens on the first move after the rest, even a move of 2 px or less. Without that, a datum resting exactly on a band edge (the acceptance bar probe) changed on the first 1 px step.\n12:- **Tests:** five browser tests in `test/browser/chart/review6.browser.test.ts`:\n21:### 2. L4 on a prefers-color-scheme change, fixed in CSS (`src/theme/`)\n22:- **Stylesheet (`css.ts`):** the `.axylo` private defaults are now `light-dark(light, dark)`, so they switch in the frame the media query does. Fixed sets remain under `[data-axylo-scheme=\"light\"]` and `[data-axylo-scheme=\"dark\"]`. The comment says `light-dark()` is supported by the current and previous major versions of the four browsers in spec 2.3.\n23:- **Resolution (`resolve.ts`):** when the chart's computed `color-scheme` is anything but `normal` and no `--axylo-background` decides, no `data-axylo-scheme` is written. The per-series properties were already references, not frozen colours.\n26:- **Canvas:** it still repaints when the change event arrives, one frame behind; a comment in `controller.ts` says so, and AX141 is judged then.\n27:- **Tests:**\n30:- **Tests changed:** three render tests and two of my chart tests expected the attribute in \"page sets color-scheme\" cases. They now expect none, which is the design change, not a loosened check.\n32:### 3. Two-tone focus ring (palette review B1)\n33:- **Datum ring (`core/focus.ts`):** a 4 px background-colour surround with the 2 px focus colour on top, i.e. 1 px of background on each side. Corners are closed, the ring is kept inside the plot's box, and the tooltip's avoid-box grows by the surround (`RING_REACH` 10).\n34:- **Plot outline (`css.ts`):** an inset `box-shadow` in the background colour under the 2 px outline. `forced-color-adjust: none` keeps it in forced colours, where both tokens are already system colours.\n35:- **Tests:**\n38:- The acceptance A2 tests still pass.\n40:### 4. Untitled chart named by its target's id (React review C6)\n41:- `Host.targetId`, from `root.id` in `chart.ts`, is used for the diagnostic chart name and for the internal-error delivery. The allocated id stays for the DOM relationships.\n42:- Node tests in `snapshot.test.ts`: \"sessions\" when the target has that id, the allocated id otherwise. `test/core/host.ts` has a new `targetId` option.\n44:### Edits outside `src/core` and `src/dom`\n45:- `src/theme/css.ts`: the token blocks and the ring surround.\n46:- `src/theme/resolve.ts`: the scheme attribute rule only.\n47:- `test/theme/review.test.ts`, `test/browser/render/scheme.browser.test.ts` (new), and the expectations in `test/browser/render/theme.browser.test.ts` and `review.browser.test.ts`.\n48:- `test/browser/chart/util.ts`: `AXYLO_BUNDLE` now also reaches the render suites, without the renderer switch.\n49:- `palette.ts` and `test/theme/palette.test.ts` show as modified in the tree, but those are the palette author's changes, not mine.\n51:### Runs (last lines, final build)\n52:- **Type check:** clean.\n55:- **Node suite without acceptance:** `Test Files 2 failed | 44 passed (46)`, `Tests 2 failed | 791 passed (793)`. Neither failure is mine:\n58:- **My browser directories, SVG:** `Test Files 14 passed (14)`, `Tests 193 passed (193)`.\n59:- **My browser directories, canvas:** `Test Files 14 passed (14)`, `Tests 193 passed (193)`.\n60:- **Render (browser):** `Test Files 6 passed | 1 skipped (7)`, `Tests 86 passed | 1 skipped (87)`.\n61:- **Theme (Node):** `Test Files 3 passed (3)`, `Tests 52 passed (52)`.\n62:- **Browser acceptance, SVG:** `Test Files 13 passed (13)`, `Tests 555 passed (555)`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"node --expose-gc - <<'AXYLO_REVIEW_STDIN'\nconst { buildSync, build } = require('esbuild');\nconst { execFileSync } = require('node:child_process');\nconst path = require('node:path');\nconst assert = require('node:assert/strict');\nconst cwd = process.cwd();\nfunction load(source, define = {__DEV__:'true'}, extra = {}) {\n  const b = buildSync({stdin:{contents:source,loader:'ts',resolveDir:cwd},bundle:true,write:false,format:'cjs',platform:'node',target:'es2022',define,logLevel:'silent',...extra});\n  return evaluate(b.outputFiles[0].text);\n}\nfunction evaluate(js){const m={exports:{}};new Function('module','exports','require',js)(m,m.exports,require);return m.exports;}\nconst fromHost=\\\"export {record,lastModel} from './packages/axylo/test/core/host';\\\";\nconst fromPublic=\\\"export {validate} from './packages/axylo/src/index';\\\";\nconst opts=(data,extra={})=>({title:'Review',data,x:'x',y:'y',...extra});\nconst rows=(xs)=>xs.map(x=>({x,y:x*10,z:x*100}));\nconst kinds=['line','area','bar','scatter','donut'];\nfunction hover(r,ref){let out;const off=r.controller.handle.on('hover',v=>out=v);r.controller.actions.hover(ref);off();return out;}\nfunction alignedXs(r){return [...r.committed.view.frame.x.values];}\nfunction hoverX(r,x,key='y'){return hover(r,{kind:'aligned',seriesKey:key,x});}\nfunction codes(c){return c.diagnostics.map(d=>d.code+(d.field?':'+d.field:''));}\n\nconst {record,lastModel,validate}=load(fromHost+fromPublic);\n{\n  let armed=false, calls=0;\n  const r=record('line',opts(rows([0,1,2]),{y:{field:'y',tickFormat(v){calls++;if(armed){armed=false;r.controller.handle.append(rows([4]),{keep:1});}return String(v);}}}));\n  r.frames();armed=true;\n  r.controller.handle.append(rows([3]),{keep:1});\n  r.frames(1);\n  console.log('tick re-entry',JSON.stringify({calls,armed,pending:r.pending,display:alignedXs(r),hover:hoverX(r,3),rows:r.controller.handle.__dev.retainedRows()}));\n  r.frames();console.log('tick next',alignedXs(r),hoverX(r,4));\n}\nfor (const mode of ['pending without frames','displayed with frames','displayed without frames','no initial frame']) {\n  const r=record('line',opts(rows([0,1])));\n  if(mode\"'!=='\"'no initial frame') r.frames();\n  r.controller.handle.append(rows([2]),{keep:1});\n  if(mode.startsWith('displayed')) r.frames();\n  r.controller.actions.pause(true);\n  for(let x=3;x<=503;x++){\n    r.controller.handle.append(rows([x]),{keep:1});\n    if(mode==='displayed with frames')r.frames();\n  }\n  console.log('pause retention',mode,r.controller.handle.__dev.retainedRows(),r.pending);\n}\n{\n  const seed=Array.from({length:8},(_,i)=>({x:0,s:'S'+i,y:i,z:i+1}));\n  const r=record('line',opts(seed,{series:'s'}));\n  r.frames();\n  r.controller.handle.append([{x:1,s:'S0',y:1,z:5}]);\n  r.frames();\n  r.controller.actions.pause(true);\n  r.controller.handle.append([{x:2,s:'S8',y:2,z:6}]);\n  const c=r.controller.handle;\n  const before=codes(c);let strict;\n  try{c.update({strict:true});strict='accepted';}catch(e){strict=e.message;}\n  c.update({strict:false});\n  c.update({y:'z'});\n  console.log('held diagnostics',JSON.stringify({before,strict,after:codes(c)}));\n}\n{\n  const r=record('line',opts([{x:0,y:0,z:NaN},{x:1,y:1,z:1}]));\n  const c=r.controller.handle;\n  r.frames();\n  c.append([{x:2,y:2,z:2}]); r.frames();\n  r.controller.actions.pause(true);\n  c.append([{x:3,y:3,z:3}],{keep:1});\n  let seen=[];\n  c.update({y:'z',onDiagnostic(d){seen.push(d.code);if(d.code==='AX103')r.controller.actions.pause(false);}});\n  r.frames();\n  console.log('reencode resume from diagnostic',JSON.stringify({seen,paused:r.committed.paused,x:alignedXs(r),diag:codes(c),pending:r.pending}));\n}\n{\n  const r=record('line',opts(rows([0,1])));const c=r.controller.handle;\n  r.frames();c.append(rows([2]),{keep:1});r.frames();r.controller.actions.pause(true);\n  c.append(rows([3]),{keep:1});c.__dev.fail('view');r.controller.actions.pause(false);r.frames();\n  c.__dev.fail(null);c.append(rows([4]),{keep:1});r.frames();const ready=alignedXs(r);\n  c.update({title:'after append'});r.frames();\n  console.log('failed resume with recovery append',JSON.stringify({ready,after:alignedXs(r),hover:hoverX(r,3),pending:r.pending}));\n}\n{\n  const r=record('line',opts(rows([0,1,2,3])));\n  r.frames(); const c=r.controller.handle; const got=[];\n  c.on('zoom',w=>got.push(w));\n  c.update({onDiagnostic(d){if(d.field==='zoom'&&d.code==='AX112')c.zoom([1,2]);}});\n  c.zoom([.5,2.5]); console.log('plain zoom',got);\n}\nAXYLO_REVIEW_STDIN\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
