{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -A16 -B6 'interface (RowSource|PointSeries|PointFrame|DatumText|DatumRef|ReaderModel)|type DatumRef|P[1357] ' packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts docs/02-product-spec.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/02-product-spec.md-235-## 5. Performance budgets\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-236-\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-237-These numbers are provisional. They are design targets taken from Phase 1's order-of-magnitude measurements, and they become release gates only after the benchmark harness built in M0 has measured a working Axylo slice in M1 and the limits have been recalibrated and frozen (plan, M1 and M6). Each budget names its workload, metric and statistic so that two people measuring the same build get the same verdict.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-238-\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-239-| ID | Workload | Metric | Statistic | Provisional limit | Phase 1 reference |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-240-|---|---|---|---|---|---|\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:241:| P1 | `trend` (3×120), default options, reference desktop | Main-thread task time from the call until the chart is complete | Median of 20 runs | 10 ms | Not comparable across libraries below about 35 ms with the Phase 1 method |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-242-| P2 | One series, 100,000 and 1,000,000 points, typed columns | Same | Median of 20 | 60 ms and 250 ms | See 01, section 5.3: uPlot and tuned Chart.js are the fastest measured |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:243:| P3 | 600-point window, one appended point per display frame at 60 Hz, driven by an independent clock | Main-thread task time per update (per run: task time in the window divided by the number of updates); and frames later than 25 ms | Median over runs; count per 300 frames | 2 ms; 0 | See 01, section 5.3 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-244-| P4 | Pointer moved across a 100,000-point chart | Time from input to the frame showing the matching readout | 95th percentile | One frame (16.7 ms at 60 Hz) | Not measured in Phase 1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:245:| P5 | 24 `trend` charts created on one page, each tile 340 × 200 px | Total main-thread task time | Median of 20 | 200 ms | Not measured in Phase 1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-246-| P6 | Download | Minified and gzipped bytes, CSS included | Exact | DX7 | 01, section 1.4 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-247-| P8 | 40 compact charts created on one page, each 160 × 48 px with one series | Total main-thread task time | Median of 20 | 80 ms | Not measured in Phase 1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:248:| P7 | Memory | Bytes owned by Axylo beyond the caller's columns for 1,000,000 points; heap trend over 1,000 create–destroy cycles | Measured after forced collection | At most 1× the size of the caller's two columns; no upward slope | Not measured in Phase 1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-249-\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-250-Three rules hold whatever the numbers become:\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-251-\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-252-1. Budgets apply to default options. Finding D8 showed libraries that are fast only for authors who know which options to set.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-253-2. Budgets are absolute, on named hardware profiles. Comparison libraries, uPlot above all, are measured in the same runs and published beside Axylo, but a ratio to another library is not a gate: it would reward leaving out work that library does not do.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-254-3. The accessibility layer is on in every measured configuration.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-255-\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-256-## 6. Decisions and the findings behind them\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-257-\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-258-\"Status\" records what the reviews changed.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-259-\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-260-| Decision | What decided it | Status after review |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-261-|---|---|---|\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-262-| Diagnostics are a first-class feature with codes | R5: none of the ten named the field, the row or the problem. | Kept. Severity and delivery rewritten (3.5): readers are told too, and production builds are not silent. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-263-| Calendar dates, instants and wall-clock times are different types | R3: given instants, six libraries show a daily value on a different day in some zones, which is correct for instants and wrong for dates; given date strings, most of them get it right. The gap is that nothing says which one the author meant. | Kept, sharpened. The test now separates the types, and a hint fires when instants look like dates. Default zone for instants: the viewer's, with the zone always visible. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md-264-| Accessibility is in the core, on by default | R11–R13. | Kept. The table is built on demand, not eagerly. |\n--\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts-81-  readonly dateUnit: 'day' | 'month' | 'year' | null;\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts-82-  /** For 'category': true when the author declared the categories ordered, so the axis may be thinned (spec L1). */\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts-83-  readonly ordered: boolean;\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts-84-}\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts-85-\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts-86-/** The caller's data behind a frame, for events and for the table's provenance. */\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts:87:export interface RowSource {\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts-88-  /** The caller's row at a source index (materialized on demand for typed columns), or null if it is no longer retained. */\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts-89-  rowAt(sourceIndex: number): unknown;\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts-90-}\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts-91-\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts-92-/** One series of an aligned frame: a y value and a state for every x slot. */\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts-93-export interface Series {\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts-94-  /** Stable identity: the series value (long form) or the field name 