{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'DX7|P7|size-limit|recalibrat|provisional' STATUS.md docs/04-plan-performance.md bench/src/decision.js\nnl -ba packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts | sed -n '1,160p'\nrg -n 'snapshot|retire\\\\(' packages/axylo/src/data/store.ts | tail -15\nrg -n 'SLOT_(VALUE|GAP|NO_ROW)|overlay' packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"bench/src/decision.js:16:/** Two columns of 1,000,000 Float64 values: the caller's columns that P7's thresholds are a share of. */\nbench/src/decision.js:17:const P7_COLUMNS = 2 * 8 * 1_000_000;\nbench/src/decision.js:33:  { id: 'P7-mem', budget: 'P7', family: 'budget', workload: 'mem', params: { size: '1x1000000', gaps: false }, metric: 'ownedBytes', unit: 'bytes', swi: 0.10 * P7_COLUMNS, tol: 0.05 * P7_COLUMNS },\nbench/src/decision.js:34:  { id: 'P7-lifecycle', budget: 'P7', family: 'budget', workload: 'lifecycle', params: { fixture: 'trend', cycles: 2500 }, metric: 'heapGrowth', unit: 'x', kind: 'gate', gate: 0.01 },\nSTATUS.md:39:Owner decisions on 2026-11-18: palette candidate B adopted (9861f54); size targets 96 KiB everything and 80 KiB line only (spec DX7); licence stays MIT with holder \"The Axylo authors\"; Playwright browser downloads allowed (Firefox and WebKit installed under ~/.cache/ms-playwright; the owner installed WebKit's system libraries); no screen-reader rehearsal for 1.0 (state it as not done, do not block on it); the React adapter is removed from 1.0 (bf93e1a; last state at dac5664; adapters for React, Vue, Svelte later; plain TypeScript for now).\nSTATUS.md:41:State at a518cbb (coordinator runs; not a recorded run): type check clean; Node suite 1 known failure (the kept P7 memory test); core browser suites 834 pass, 1 skipped, on the restructured build with palette B (run before the React removal, which does not touch them); distribution 83 Node and 26 browser pass; docs 218 unit pass (160 browser per the author); benchmark harness 97 pure tests pass. Sizes from the packed files: everything 104.24 KiB (target 96), line only 87.50 (target 80), donut only 75.32, validate only 20.40.\nSTATUS.md:45:For the core's author after the final reviews (one pass): review findings; the benchmark hooks in `src/core/instrument.ts` (`series[i].breaks`, `describe().plot`, `memory()` returning `{ bytes, buffers }`, `series[i].keptBasis === 'window'` for streams); the unexplained 24-chart resize mismatch (marks up to 13 px from the reported domain); library oddities from the docs author (`wp/docs.fix.report.md`: a wide-row summary uses the field key and puts the unit on the minimum only; the hidden plot control reads \"No data\" in the too-small state; AX199 wording); a size pass toward 96 and 80 KiB; the deferred P7 and scatter-pick items. Small record fixes for the palette author: `wp/palette-b.review.md` findings 1 to 6 (decision line 14 still says nobody else reviewed B).\nSTATUS.md:59:3. Record every configuration on a quiet tree (`node acceptance/run.mjs …`; add Firefox and WebKit configurations), have the matrix's author re-merge (engines; React rows gone; DX1, DX7, DX8 amended; A3 rehearsal recorded as not done by the owner's decision), run the checker.\ndocs/04-plan-performance.md:5:The repeated improvement work starts when the TypeScript release from [03-plan-typescript-release.md](03-plan-typescript-release.md) works end to end, and that release is its baseline. The **measurement harness is built earlier, in milestone M0**, because the release's own budgets (P1–P7 in [02-product-spec.md](02-product-spec.md)) cannot be checked without it and two design decisions in M1 depend on its numbers.\ndocs/04-plan-performance.md:35:| W-mem | Memory, as defined in 3.1 | – | Tab memory; slow leak | P7 |\ndocs/04-plan-performance.md:139:### 5.1 Declared endpoints (provisional until the pilot)\ndocs/04-plan-performance.md:155:| P7 | `mem`, 1 × 1,000,000 | Bytes owned beyond the caller's columns | 10% of the two columns | 5% of the two columns |\ndocs/04-plan-performance.md:156:| P7 | `lifecycle` | Heap after forced collection, cycles 1,500–2,000 against 2,000–2,500 | n/a | Growth above 1% between the two windows |\ndocs/04-plan-performance.md:178:| Before a release | Full set, plus Edge on Windows, Safari by hand, the phone profile when available, and all comparison libraries | Budgets P1–P7 and the previous release | A failed budget blocks the release, or the budget is changed in the spec with the measurements and a written reason. Never silently. |\ndocs/04-plan-performance.md:217:| What does data transfer cost? | Time and peak memory to move columns into WebAssembly memory and results back, included in the end-to-end number. If columns live in WebAssembly memory to avoid copies, the effect on `update`, `append` and P7 is measured too. |\n     1\timport { BufferWindow } from './store-window';\n     2\timport { SLOT_NO_ROW, type AlignedFrame, type RowSource, type Series, type XColumn } from '../core/contracts';\n     3\t\n     4\tinterface OpenSlot {\n     5\t  readonly index: number;\n     6\t  exposed: boolean;\n     7\t  claimed: boolean;\n     8\t  readonly y: number;\n     9\t  readonly slot: number;\n    10\t  readonly row: number;\n    11\t}\n    12\t\n    13\ttype SeriesDescription = Omit<Series, 'y' | 'slot' | 'row'>;\n    14\texport interface SeriesBuffers {\n    15\t  description: SeriesDescription;\n    16\t  y: Float64Array;\n    17\t  slot: Uint8Array;\n    18\t  row: Int32Array;\n    19\t  tail?: OpenSlot;\n    20\t}\n    21\t\n    22\tfunction buffers(description: SeriesDescription, capacity: number): SeriesBuffers {\n    23\t  return { description, y: new Float64Array(capacity), slot: new Uint8Array(capacity), row: new Int32Array(capacity) };\n    24\t}\n    25\t\n    26\texport class FrameBuffers {\n    27\t  x: Float64Array;\n    28\t  observed: Uint8Array;\n    29\t  private categoryPositions = new Float64Array();\n    30\t  readonly series = new Map<string, SeriesBuffers>();\n    31\t  private range: BufferWindow;\n    32\t\n    33\t  get start(): number { return this.range.start; }\n    34\t  get end(): number { return this.range.end; }\n    35\t  set end(end: number) { this.range.end = end; }\n    36\t  distinct: number;\n    37\t\n    38\t  constructor(frame?: AlignedFrame, positions?: Float64Array, order: Int32Array | null = null) {\n    39\t    this.range = new BufferWindow(0, frame?.length ?? 0);\n    40\t    this.distinct = 0;\n    41\t    const capacity = this.end + Math.max(16, Math.ceil(this.end / 8));\n    42\t    this.x = new Float64Array(capacity);\n    43\t    this.observed = new Uint8Array(capacity);\n    44\t    if (!frame || !positions) return;\n    45\t    this.x.set(frame.x.values);\n    46\t    let slot = 0;\n    47\t    const length = order?.length ?? positions.length;\n    48\t    for (let i = 0; i < length; i++) {\n    49\t      const x = positions[order?.[i] ?? i]!;\n    50\t      while (slot < this.end && this.x[slot]! < x) slot++;\n    51\t      if (slot < this.end && this.x[slot] === x && !this.observed[slot]) {\n    52\t        this.observed[slot] = 1;\n    53\t        this.distinct++;\n    54\t      }\n    55\t    }\n    56\t    for (const { row, slot, y, ...description } of frame.series) {\n    57\t      const series = buffers(description, capacity);\n    58\t      series.y.set(y);\n    59\t      series.slot.set(slot);\n    60\t      if (row) series.row.set(row);\n    61\t      else for (let i = 0; i < this.end; i++) series.row[i] = i;\n    62\t      this.series.set(description.key, series);\n    63\t    }\n    64\t  }\n    65\t\n    66\t  fork(): FrameBuffers {\n    67\t    const draft = Object.assign(Object.create(FrameBuffers.prototype) as FrameBuffers, this, {\n    68\t      range: this.range.fork(),\n    69\t      series: new Map(Array.from(this.series, ([key, series]) => [key, { ...series }])),\n    70\t    });\n    71\t    return draft;\n    72\t  }\n    73\t\n    74\t  get hasCompetingWrites(): boolean { return this.range.hasCompetingWrites; }\n    75\t\n    76\t  reserve(extra: number): boolean {\n    77\t    const capacity = this.range.reserve(extra, this.x.length);\n    78\t    if (capacity) this.resize(capacity, extra);\n    79\t    // A rival may have claimed the base's tail. Reconstruct that tail before this\n    80\t    // draft can publish a longer view in which the old slot is no longer special.\n    81\t    else for (const series of this.series.values()) {\n    82\t      if (series.tail?.claimed) this.copySeries(series);\n    83\t    }\n    84\t    return capacity !== 0;\n    85\t  }\n    86\t\n    87\t  shrink(): void {\n    88\t    const capacity = this.range.compact(this.x.length);\n    89\t    if (capacity) this.resize(capacity, 0);\n    90\t  }\n    91\t\n    92\t  private resize(capacity: number, extra: number): void {\n    93\t    const { start, end } = this;\n    94\t    const x = new Float64Array(capacity);\n    95\t    const observed = new Uint8Array(capacity);\n    96\t    x.set(this.x.subarray(start, end));\n    97\t    observed.set(this.observed.subarray(start, end));\n    98\t    this.x = x;\n    99\t    this.observed = observed;\n   100\t    if (this.categoryPositions.length > capacity) this.categoryPositions = new Float64Array();\n   101\t    for (const [key, previous] of this.series) {\n   102\t      const series = buffers(previous.description, capacity);\n   103\t      series.y.set(previous.y.subarray(start, end));\n   104\t      series.slot.set(previous.slot.subarray(start, end));\n   105\t      series.row.set(previous.row.subarray(start, end));\n   106\t      restoreTail(previous.tail, series, end - start - 1);\n   107\t      this.series.set(key, series);\n   108\t    }\n   109\t    this.range.rebase(extra);\n   110\t  }\n   111\t\n   112\t  copySeries(series: SeriesBuffers): SeriesBuffers {\n   113\t    const copy = buffers(series.description, this.x.length);\n   114\t    const { start, end } = this;\n   115\t    copy.y.set(series.y.subarray(start, end), start);\n   116\t    copy.slot.set(series.slot.subarray(start, end), start);\n   117\t    copy.row.set(series.row.subarray(start, end), start);\n   118\t    restoreTail(series.tail, copy, end - 1);\n   119\t    this.series.set(series.description.key, copy);\n   120\t    return copy;\n   121\t  }\n   122\t\n   123\t  writeTail(series: SeriesBuffers, hasCompetingWrites: boolean): SeriesBuffers {\n   124\t    const tail = series.tail;\n   125\t    // An advanced preview can expose this slot in the middle of its view. After a draw\n   126\t    // has requested a column, a fill copies that series' window to protect the issued view.\n   127\t    // Between draws the first writer claims the open slot and only touches the appended rows.\n   128\t    if (!tail || tail.exposed || hasCompetingWrites) return this.copySeries(series);\n   129\t    tail.claimed = true;\n   130\t    series.tail = undefined;\n   131\t    return series;\n   132\t  }\n   133\t\n   134\t  addSeries(description: SeriesDescription, zero: boolean): SeriesBuffers {\n   135\t    const series = buffers(description, this.x.length);\n   136\t    series.row.fill(-1, this.start, this.end);\n   137\t    if (!zero) {\n   138\t      series.y.fill(NaN, this.start, this.end);\n   139\t      series.slot.fill(SLOT_NO_ROW, this.start, this.end);\n   140\t    }\n   141\t    this.series.set(description.key, series);\n   142\t    return series;\n   143\t  }\n   144\t\n   145\t  trim(keep: number | undefined, evict: (x: number, observed: boolean) => void): void {\n   146\t    if (keep === undefined || keep >= this.distinct) return;\n   147\t    while (this.start < this.end && (this.distinct > keep || !this.observed[this.start])) {\n   148\t      const observed = this.observed[this.start] === 1;\n   149\t      if (observed) this.distinct--;\n   150\t      evict(this.x[this.start]!, observed);\n   151\t      this.range.start++;\n   152\t    }\n   153\t  }\n   154\t\n   155\t  frame(previous: AlignedFrame, axis: XColumn, source: RowSource, open: (key: string) => boolean): AlignedFrame {\n   156\t    const { start, end } = this;\n   157\t    let positions = this.x.subarray(start, end);\n   158\t    if (axis.kind === 'category' && positions[0]) {\n   159\t      if (this.categoryPositions.length < positions.length) {\n   160\t        const capacity = Math.max(16, positions.length * 2);\n457:    this.current = this.snapshot(frame);\n488:  retire(revision: number): void { this.revisions.retire(Math.min(revision, this.current.revision)); }\n580:    draft.current = draft.snapshot(built.frame);\n805:  private snapshot(frame: AlignedFrame): AlignedFrame {\n1025:    this.current = this.snapshot(this.current);\n57:export const SLOT_VALUE = 0;         // a finite number\n60:export const SLOT_NO_ROW = 3;        // this series has no observation at this x and none was expected; neighbours may be joined across it\n61:export const SLOT_GAP = 4;           // an expected step of this series is absent (AX105): never joined across\n65: * `missing: 'zero'` on a value field is applied by normalization: slots that would be SLOT_NULL, SLOT_NO_ROW,\n66: * SLOT_GAP or SLOT_ABSENT_FIELD become SLOT_VALUE with y = 0 and row = -1. SLOT_INVALID is never turned into zero.\n104:  /** y per slot. NaN wherever `slot` is not SLOT_VALUE. May be a view on the caller's typed column. */\n167:  /** NaN where `slot` is not SLOT_VALUE. */\n179: * Join rule for lines and areas (spec F2). Two consecutive SLOT_VALUE slots i < j of one series are joined\n180: * if and only if every slot strictly between them is SLOT_NO_ROW. A value with no joined neighbour on either\n259: * for k = 0) its lower boundary; likewise `negative`. A component that is not SLOT_VALUE contributes zero\n574:  /** Draws or clears (null) the overlay without redrawing the scene. */\n575:  drawOverlay(overlay: Overlay | null, bindings: PaintBindings, theme: ResolvedTheme, devicePixelRatio: number): void;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
