1},{x:'B',y:2},{x:'C',y:3},{x:'D',y:4}];\n const received=[];\n const o=kind==='donut'?{title:'D',data:d,label:'x',value:'y'}:opts(d);\n const r=record(kind,{...o,strict:true,onDiagnostic:d=>received.push(d)});r.frames();\n const old=r.committed.view;\n r.controller.handle.zoom(['B','C']);r.controller.handle.zoom(null);r.frames();\n assert.equal(r.committed.view,old);\n assert.deepEqual(received.map(d=>[d.code,d.field]),[['AX150','zoom']]);\n}\n{\n const r=record('bar',opts([{x:'A',y:null},{x:'B',y:null}]));r.frames();\n assert.equal(lastModel(r).message,null);\n assert(r.draws.at(-1).marks.some(m=>m.type==='rects'&&m.variant==='missing'&&m.xywh.length===8));\n}\n{\n const r=record('line',{data:rows([0,1]),x:'x',y:'y'},{targetId:'sessions'});r.frames();\n assert.equal(r.controller.handle.diagnostics.find(d=>d.code==='AX140').chart,'sessions');\n r.controller.handle.update({title:'Traffic',data:[{x:0,y:0},{x:1,y:NaN}]});\n assert.equal(r.controller.handle.diagnostics.find(d=>d.code==='AX103').chart,'Traffic');\n}\nconsole.log('scatter value scale, category/donut no-op, all-missing bars, target-id/title names verified');\nAXYLO_REVIEW_STDIN\"","aggregated_output":"pending append at Pause, zero-size clears\nold option resubmissions and static labels fixed\nold four AX160 scenarios fixed\nscatter value scale, category/donut no-op, all-missing bars, target-id/title names verified\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"agent_message","text":"# Final review of `a518cbb`\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **B · A frame can lose its source rows while it is drawing. Ran in Node.** Draw a line at x `[0,1,2]`, then append `3` with `keep: 1`. In the tick formatter for that frame, append `4` with `keep: 1`. The first frame draws `3`, but hovering it returns `index: 3, row: null`. Layout calls the formatter after publication has started, and the nested append can retire the in-flight revision. I also reproduced a superseded frame’s failure putting a newer valid update into the AX199 error state. Destroying from a hover callback during commit retained the caller’s data after forced collection because `showing()` ran after `destroy()`. DX5 and plan §1.5 require a coherent publication and complete teardown. Pin the in-flight snapshot through publication, finish it before delivering interaction callbacks, and prevent a stale or destroyed generation from publishing state or errors. [controller.ts](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:982) · [Interaction commit](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1541)\n\n2. **B · Pause defeats `keep` with or without frame callbacks. Ran in Node.** Draw `[0,1]`, append `2` with `keep: 1`, pause before that frame, then append `3` through `503` with `keep: 1` and run no frames. The store retains **502 rows**. Drawing `2` before pausing and running a frame after every subsequent append also retains **502 rows**. The first sequence pins a pending revision that `release()` never freezes. In the second, each redraw of the same paused snapshot raises the retention baseline. Plan §1.5 and P7 require bounded retention. Give both pending and displayed snapshots independent ownership when they pin history, and reset the retention baseline only when the displayed data revision changes. [release and showing](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1353)\n\n3. **B · Recovery after a failed Resume can roll the chart back to retired data. Ran in Node.** Display `2`, pause, append `3` with `keep: 1`, and inject a view failure on Resume. Remove the fault, append `4` with `keep: 1`, and draw. The chart shows `4`. A title-only update then puts `3` back on screen, and its hover returns `row: null`. The successful append leaves `held` pointing to the older revision, which `resumable()` later promotes. This breaks call order and provenance under DX5 and plan §1.5. A successful append after failed Resume must consume or supersede the held revision in the same acceptance step. [resumable](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:717) · [append acceptance](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:675)\n\n4. **B · The first append exceeds the retained-memory budget. Ran in Node with forced collection.** Open a one-million-point line over two borrowed `Float64Array` columns and append one row. The store retains **24,750,128 bytes beyond the caller’s 16,000,000 bytes**, before counting the whole chart. I also reproduced retention of the original caller column after both `keep: 2` and explicit replacement. A locale change that rebuilt the formatters made it collectible. P7 and plan §2.2 require a cheaper handoff. Keep the borrowed prefix with an appendable tail, avoid dense identity indexes for untouched rows, and free the original data and table-bearing formatter state when their snapshots retire. [Store allocation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:38) · [Formatter construction](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:925) · [Failing budget test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/data/streaming-storage.test.ts:88)\n\n5. **B · Both DX7 download targets are exceeded. Ran against the installed distribution fixture.** Bundle the documented npm example and then a consumer exporting everything. With CSS included as shipped, the results are **89,605 B** against **81,920 B** for line only and **106,738 B** against **98,304 B** for everything. The installed production ESM matched the in-memory rebuild byte for byte. The named kinds tree-shake, so the remaining work is to reduce the code and stylesheet reachable from each entry point and enforce the existing byte targets on the packed artifact. [Public entry points](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/index.ts:19) · [Size measurement](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/scripts/size.mjs:60)\n\n6. **M · Paused data is only partly validated and re-encoded. Ran in Node.** Hold a ninth series while paused. The append reports AX130, but `update({strict: true})` succeeds, and changing the y field drops AX130. If a new-field AX103 handler calls Resume during re-encoding, the chart switches to running while the arrivals stay held. On scatter, re-encoding a paused snapshot also drops a row such as `{x: 1, y: null, z: 11}` when changing `y` to `z`, because `freeze()` only visits drawable points. A missing-field AX101 can likewise survive a valid held append and Resume. This violates I6, DX5 and §3.5. Build and validate both windows, preserve their complete source rows, and accept the pair before invoking callbacks. [Paused re-encoding](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:555) · [AX101 recovery](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:639) · [Row freezing](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:693)\n\n7. **M · Exceptional call validation disagrees with `validate()` and bypasses `strict`. Ran in Node on all five kinds.** Supply an unknown option `palete` and a row whose x or label getter throws. `validate()` returns AX150 followed by AX199. Create reports only AX199 and returns an error-state chart even with `strict: true`, although it already found a call-origin AX150. A strict update with a throwing row getter also replaces the last good display with the internal-error state. Share call preparation and exception classification, retain findings collected before failure, and apply strict rejection before changing the accepted chart. [Controller exception path](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:500) · [Static validation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/stages.ts:156)\n\n8. **M · A scatter pointer move can do work proportional to the data. Ran in Node.** Pick the centre of a 20 px radius ring containing 32,000 points. The grid examines **32,048 candidates**. In a separate 50,000-point chart, picking the last row caused the controller to read **50,000 row indexes** to build the hover event, even though the lookup already knew the point’s index. The controller builds that payload even with no subscriber. This leaves plan §2.1’s bounded lookup unmet. I1 and P4 browser latency remain unmeasured. Reuse the located index for exact event values, skip unused payloads, and test a bounded nearest-point and coincidence query against adversarial point layouts. [Grid search](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter-grid.ts:203) · [Event lookup](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1449)\n\n9. **M · Short plots silently skip the reserved readout. Ran in Node.** At a 330 × 205 recording-host container, a line commits a 283 × 92 plot with `readout: false`. A donut commits a 330 × 118 plot with the same result in a shorter container. The extra condition at 80 px selects a floating tooltip even though I1 and decision 0004 rule 5 require the strip below 140 px. Treat the strip as required space and evaluate L8 on the remaining plot, with the mode selected from geometry that excludes the strip’s own effect. That is my reading of how the two rules should interact. [Readout decision](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1193)\n\n10. **M · A tooltip corridor can keep a datum after eviction. Reasoned from the interaction path.** Rest on a bar whose tooltip is beside it, begin moving through the rule 3b corridor, then append with `keep` so that bar leaves the window. A same-epoch commit repicks the pointer and remaps some references, but keeps the old corridor and its target. The next move inside the old hull suppresses picking and restores the evicted target. This breaks I1 and decision 0004 rule 3b. Invalidate or revalidate the corridor, held tooltip and resting datum with the new snapshot and layout before allowing them to override picking. [Corridor hit test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:872) · [Interaction commit](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1541)\n\n11. **M · Cached tick layouts can lose AX160 and the reader note. Ran in Node.** Use a throwing y tick formatter, draw, set `state: 'loading'`, then clear `state` at the same measured size. The same fallback tick labels return without a formatter call, AX160, or the F12 note. The loading frame clears the diagnostic bucket while `lastLayout` keeps the fallback labels. Store findings with each cached layout and publish the findings for the layout actually used. [Layout cache and bucket](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1178)\n\n12. **M · Temporal inputs remain mutable and some emitted windows cannot round-trip. Ran in Node.** Mutate a `Date` in `x.domain` from January 1 to January 3 and resubmit the option. The domain still starts on January 1. Mutate the first `Date` passed to `zoom()` and then update a reference. The window moves without a second zoom call. On an instant axis, `[t + 0.25, t + 0.75]` emits two equal `Date` values, and passing the event to another chart resets it to its full range. Snapshot option dates, keep zoom endpoints as immutable positions, and emit a numeric position when a `Date` or string cannot encode it exactly. This restores plan §1.5 and the public event contract. [Option snapshots](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/options.ts:43) · [Position conversion](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:191) · [Zoom acceptance](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:730)\n\n13. **M · Compact charts accept latent zoom and silently ignore secondary tick formats. Ran in Node on line, area and bar.** Call `zoom([1,3])` on a compact chart. It emits a zoom event for the full range, saves the requested window, and applies `[1,3]` when `compact` is later turned off. In wide mode a `y[1].tickFormat` is ignored without AX150, although `x.tickFormat` and `y[0].tickFormat` are reported. This violates §3.7 and F3. Reject compact zoom before changing state or emitting an event, and report every supplied compact tick format that has no output. [Zoom gate](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:730) · [Wide field resolution](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/options.ts:237)\n\n14. **M · Watcher setup and reattachment leave environment state behind. Ran with Node substitutes, traced browser wiring.** Make the theme observer’s `observe()` throw after its three media listeners register. All three remain registered. `chart.ts` also records its combined cleanup only after every watcher succeeds. Separately, change the font metrics while detached and reattach. The controller reruns layout, but the document measurement cache still returns the old width, **35 instead of 75** in my probe. DX5 and plan §2.2 require complete cleanup and fresh measurements. Register each cleanup as it succeeds, make the individual watcher exception-safe, and invalidate the document font cache on reattachment. [Watcher setup](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:91) · [Theme subscriptions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/watch.ts:34) · [Measurement cache](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/environment.ts:89)\n\n15. **M · Automatic numeric x domains can end between ticks. Ran in Node.** A line with x values `1.1` and `8.9` commits `[1.1,8.9]` as both its full domain and its projection. The first and last drawn ticks are `2` and `8`. I read amended F7 as covering continuous x as well as the value axis. Choose the automatic x limits with the tick set and use those limits consistently in projection, lookup and zoom clamping. [X-domain construction](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:258) · [X tick selection](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:64)\n\n16. **M · Series cues repeat earlier than F9 permits. Ran in Node.** Draw 32 compact bar series in one category. Series indexes 1 and 25 share a palette slot and pattern, as do six more pairs. The full bar chart has 32 distinct combinations. On scatter, indexes 0 and 64 share color and shape, and the scatter renderer has no dash cue. Preserve the 32 distinct bar combinations in compact mode and extend scatter’s marker cues and swatches when the current combinations run out. [Compact bar patterns](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:106) · [Series cues](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:73)\n\n## Displayed snapshots\n\nIn ordinary calls, `accepted` advances synchronously, `held` contains paused arrivals, and `drawn` supplies events until the next publication. `onScreen` pins the displayed rows or carries a frozen copy once the store retires them. An unmeasured frame clears old marks before dropping that pin. I reran the original Pause-to-Resume provenance sequence on all five kinds, and the pending-at-Pause case on line. I treated an append accepted before Pause as eligible for that pending draw. Both the paused retention failure and the re-entrant publication failure are independent of that interpretation. [Publication](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1297) · [Row ownership](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1346)\n\nThe property generator uses a single numeric line, finite increasing rows, mandatory `keep`, and at most 40 operations. Its zoom only resets to `null`. It generates replacements, but never re-encoding, destruction, formatter or event re-entry, resize, or any failure other than an injected reader fault. It compares prepared and committed views and checks hover provenance, but does not compare the actual path or caption with an independent model of the expected accepted and held windows. Its retention slack also leaves room for many excess revisions. I separately injected faults at all 14 instrumented stages and checked recovery and subsequent destroy. [Snapshot property](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/snapshot.test.ts:291)\n\n## Composition, registry and builds\n\nI loaded `08b469b` and `a518cbb` directly from Git into memory. Across 13 configurations, I compared create and append output, ordered diagnostics, scene geometry, overlays, lookup, navigation, swatches and table rows. I traced the browser slice-list and renderer wiring in source.\n\n| Kind | Composition compared with the old dispatch |\n|---|---|\n| Line, full and compact | Aligned storage, lookup and reader. Path, point, rule and band handlers cover the scene, cursor and focus. Line swatch and aligned stepping are connected. |\n| Area, full and compact | Same aligned paths, with fill, seam and edge handlers present for stacked and unstacked geometry. The swatch retains its fill and marker. |\n| Bar, full and compact | Band lookup, aligned reader, rectangles for bars and missing data, and rules for outlines and focus. Full-chart swatches use the mark patterns. |\n| Scatter | Point storage, grid lookup and scatter table, including missing observations. Single-series stepping and point swatches are connected. Both renderers supply point, rule and band handlers. |\n| Donut | Slice storage, lookup, table and summary. Arc handlers cover the ring and slice outlines, and rules cover focus. The slice list and its swatches remain wired. |\n\nI found no missing handler or reordered diagnostics caused by the split in those comparisons. The source bundle metafiles contain only the requested composition for each named chart export. `validate` reaches all pure data and view shapes, with no reader, renderer, scene or DOM modules. The shared temporal table-jump helper still goes through aligned normalization. It needs no other chart composition. [Compositions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/kinds/index.ts:1) · [Table-jump parser](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/reader/x.ts:18)\n\nThe registry comparison matched **62 diagnostic constructions from the current registry tests**, in order, and **1,740 direct constructions across all 29 codes**. Full messages, including fix and outcome text, levels, effects, origins and row samples matched. Create and `validate()` matched for the 13 titled configurations. The exceptional mismatch is finding 7. An untitled `validate()` has only the kind for its name, while create can use a target id. [Registry](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/diagnostics/registry.ts:167)\n\nThe `__DEV__ || (typeof __BENCH__ !== 'undefined' && __BENCH__)` guard folded out the instrumentation in the shipped production recipe. The production bundle contained neither hook, even with `globalThis.__AXYLO_BENCH__` set. I also ran development, a build defining only `__DEV__`, and benchmark builds with the runtime flag off and on. Ordinary strict rejection, diagnostic callbacks and AX199 recovery after a real throwing host renderer worked in both release and development. Hints reached callbacks in both and printed only in development. The internal Canvas switch remains reachable in both, as specified by decision 0002. [Controller guard](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:265) · [Hook attachment](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/instrument.ts:79) · [Build constants](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/scripts/build.mjs:44)\n\n## Verification\n\nNo files changed. `npm run typecheck` passed. The library-only serial run used Vitest with `--no-cache --configLoader runner --maxWorkers 1`. The sole failure was the typed handoff in finding 4.\n\n```text\nTest Files  1 failed | 62 passed (63)\n     Tests  1 failed | 1310 passed (1311)\n```\n\nA parallel run also failed the simplifier wall-time assertion, which passed serially. The repository-wide run hit a docs fixture that writes a temporary TypeScript config, which the read-only filesystem rejected. Browser rendering, native observer behavior, CSP and the full lifecycle heap trend were outside this run. The fixes above fit the fixed contracts.\n\n## Earlier findings\n\n| # | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Fixed with a new defect | Ran. The original summary callback aborts cleanly. Late layout and commit callbacks still break ownership. See 1. |\n| 2 | Fixed | Ran. All five kinds preserve the displayed row from Pause through Resume until the replacement draws. |\n| 3 | Fixed | Ran. Persistent primary mark and text failures hide surfaces and clear interaction. A subsequent valid update recovers. |\n| 4 | Partly | Ran. The original unpaused no-frame and failed-frame bounds hold, and a zero-size frame clears marks. Paused retention remains unbounded. See 2. |\n| 5 | Fixed with a new defect | Ran. Ordinary paused re-encoding and recovery by title update work. Recovery by append can resurrect stale data. See 3 and 6. |\n| 6 | Partly | Ran. A rejected first append leaves controls alone, and held donut errors stay off screen. Strict updates and re-encoding miss held findings. See 6. |\n| 7 | Fixed | Ran. Nested diagnostic, zoom and hover delivery preserves the original subscriber sequence. |\n| 8 | Partly | Ran. A valid kept append repairs AX101 in all five kinds when running. The equivalent paused append and Resume still leave AX101. |\n| 9 | Partly | Ran unsubscribe collection and second-`matchMedia` failure. Both passed. The outer watcher sequence can still strand registrations. See 14. |\n| 10 | Fixed | Reasoned. Theme properties and scheme are scoped to each figure, and destroying a chart removes its figure. |\n| 11 | Partly | Ran. Subsequent appends reuse spare buffers and a title change avoids normalization and summary formatting. Handoff and caller-column retention remain. See 4. |\n| 12 | Partly | Ran. Edited plain options take effect and static label edits reuse the columns. Temporal aliases remain. See 12. |\n| 13 | Fixed with a new defect | Ran. The four original AX160 cases pass. A cached layout reused after loading loses its findings. See 11. |\n| 14 | Partly | Ran. Simple AX199 delivery and `undefined`-key parity work. An exception after an option finding still breaks parity and strict rejection. See 7. |\n| 15 | Fixed | Ran. The scatter percent and ratio examples end at 100 and 1. |\n| 16 | Fixed | Ran. The original scatter and continuous-bar windows follow the latest datum. Scatter also follows a latest observation with missing y. |\n| 17 | Fixed | Ran against amended §3.6. Category and donut zoom requests report AX150 and leave the view alone. |\n| 18 | Fixed | Ran. Two null bars produce two baseline missing marks. |\n| 19 | Partly | Ran. Reattachment rereads DPR, a language update reformats and retags output, and the themed callback batch draws once. The document font cache remains stale on reattachment. See 14. |\n| 20 | Partly | Ran live host accessors and the revised Node assertions. Inspected the stronger browser assertions. The late-setup test counts frame requests but does not assert cancellation or watcher cleanup. |\n\n- **Pending replacement.** Replacing data with a stream frame pending, then appending and zooming, produced one draw of the new data. The old hover still resolved until that draw.\n- **Donut and stack readouts.** The exercised donut kept its zero and null entries separate from Other and used one fractional share digit. The mixed stack reported `5 and -2 (incomplete)` and marked the table row incomplete.\n- **Compact references.** All three variants reported AX150 and excluded the reference from the domain and drawing.\n- **Diagnostic names.** An untitled chart used `sessions` from the target id. A subsequent titled update reported its new finding under that title.\n\nI would not release this controller. A frame can publish after losing its source, paused streams can retain unbounded history, and recovery from a failed Resume can restore retired data. The typed streaming handoff and both shipped download sizes also exceed their stated budgets."}}
